1790139140129027	continuum-dev	itc:v3:AWKSTzM5JJnJPkQAAAAAQar23VW6voAAAAEyrRI		item.create	bn-2318t	{"description":"bn-gzy1 bound PR-14 reserve/commit/abort. continuum_task's region calculus has Reserve and Commit steps, but a running worker cannot drop a staged publication. It can only fail or be drained. So journals with explicit ObligationToken::abort lift as Inconclusive (Unsupported), not Conforms. The calculus also admits one staged publication per worker, and asupersync allows many tokens per task. Deliver: a WorkerStep::Abort in the calculus, with its RFC text (it is a semantic-core change: GOV §4 record plus a dedicated security review). Decide and record whether multiple staged reservations per worker are admitted. Then make the binding lift explicit aborts to Conforms, and update the START_HERE narrowing.","kind":"task","labels":["phase-b","req:phase-b","req:pr-14"],"title":"Region calculus: an explicit-abort worker step (WorkerStep::Abort) so asupersync explicit aborts lift as conforming (bn-gzy1)"}	blake3:3htL5JERSk4_8EMDOiqDrMSZafuLew4gi7Hv_G1REdM
