1790144434566692	continuum-dev	itc:v3:AWKSTzM5JJnJPkQAAAAAQar23VW6voAAAAEy7hI		item.create	bn-1i050	{"description":"bn-ujpz0's independent primitive conformance model (crates/continuum-asupersync/tests/support/primitive_conformance_model.rs) showed that the adapter's lift accepts 666 perturbed journals in 7 classes (LIFT_GAPS in tests/a7_primitive_conformance.rs) that the normative text forbids. Examples: a finalize with no drain report; a cancel-abort or timer cancel placed before the task's acknowledgement; a task completing as cancelled while it holds an obligation or an armed timer; a parked task arming a timer; a sleeping task resuming before its timer fires. Deliver: fix the lift (src/lift.rs and the family lifts) so each class is a typed Nonconformance, empty LIFT_GAPS, and keep the sweep asserting that model and lift agree. continuum-asupersync is a BOUNDARY crate, so no GOV §4 record is needed unless the change reaches continuum-task. Blocks the PR-14 exit.","kind":"task","labels":["phase-b","req:phase-b","req:pr-14","risk:high"],"title":"PR-14 lift: close the 7 gap classes the A7 conformance model found (bn-ujpz0)"}	blake3:By9dWu6WtTEikRN8ULgmLTuZgbGNtqQTFoNCrhOc8nU
