1790194197073240	continuum-dev	itc:v3:AWKSTzM5JJnJPkQAAAAAQar23VW6voAAAAEy2xM		item.comment	bn-28kv4	{"body":"6f1b7fa: cr-3hcpn4 round 7. Pack handles authorized in full (whole call denied, no partial pack); subscription full readmission per delivery; one-run minted refusal with results discarded, per-capability charge and memo; replay offers re-run through N2; profile-less delegate cannot escape a deny list. Adversarial review findings: (1) HIGH refusal poisoning a shared task FIXED (per-capability memo, no task write); (2) MED resume denial wrote budget and guard was bypassable FIXED (restore, keyed memo); (3) MED derived ws_/in_ ignored class FIXED; (4) MED create convergence and seal/diff intent FIXED; (5) LOW ctx work before denial FIXED; (6) LOW restored Completed tasks re-run on read DEFERRED (pre-existing, authorized reads, needs a cache design); (7) LOW handler denial binds the idempotency key DEFERRED (unbinding breaks the ratified G1-03 key-reuse contract). just check exit 0."}	blake3:9fiykCbVm7Hh3Sd8aw7O4a4nrI1B4pyad1kiHu_BlI8
1790194234670581	continuum-dev	itc:v3:AWKSTzM5JJnJPkQAAAAAQar23VW6voAAAAEy3BM		item.comment	bn-28kv4	{"body":"Lead: adversarial finding 7 (a handler CapabilityDenied binds the idempotency key, so handler and admission denials are distinguishable) is ACCEPTED as a documented residual. The ratified G1-03 contract (a reused key with a different body answers IdempotencyKeyReused) wins, and the distinction reveals only that the request passed admission. Finding 6 (restored Completed tasks re-explore on every result/await, uncharged) is a new follow-up bone."}	blake3:0K6HbaWyE1CMPQmu-tBToGLJunPhiZqg9ERG5Hd2pZU
1790194236829162	continuum-dev	itc:v3:AWKSTzM5JJnJPkQAAAAAQar23VW6voAAAAEy3RM		item.create	bn-2ot3g	{"description":"bn-28kv4's adversarial review found that a Completed task restored from the durable store re-runs its exploration on every verification.result or verification.await, uncharged. This predates bn-28kv4 and is reachable only by callers already authorized for the task, but it is unaccounted work. Deliver: a durable, content-addressed result cache, keyed by the task's run identity, so a restored completed task answers without re-exploring; or charge re-exploration to the caller's budget or quota. Add a regression that counts explorations across repeated result calls after a restart.","kind":"task","labels":["security","risk:high","req:phase-b"],"title":"continuumd: cache or charge re-exploration of restored Completed tasks on verification.result/await (bn-28kv4 adversarial finding 6)"}	blake3:-a9RaIqhZlnQGv6g9nGepIm6MAjylokuxpr-ubZ4KcQ
1790194236869138	continuum-dev	itc:v3:AWKSTzM5JJnJPkQAAAAAQar23VW6voAAAAEy3hM		item.link	bn-2ot3g	{"link_type":"blocks","target":"bn-19p"}	blake3:QEauDi8ppTabf3brkFbr7bVEPliB38y3EPVPQKS7KCI
1790194288787109	continuum-dev	itc:v3:AWKSTzM5JJnJPkQAAAAAQar23VW6voAAAAEy3xM		item.comment	bn-36wy3	{"body":"cr-3pu5cu round 5 (th-1shbkn) fixed in 322a003. A task's own cancellation ends only by its own lifecycle cancel. The lift records this as provenance (ended_alone) and never reads it from the Cancelled state. Region events inside an own cancellation are InterruptedOwnCancel (RFC 0026 c53 item 6). The pre-review pass fixed: family presence read before the first event, complete after a phase, DeadlineIgnored, Deadline after a request. The A7 model has the same rules. Deferred: per-task indexes for the O(n) scans at cancel. just check: all pass except the lead-owned security-review-present."}	blake3:jpA9HJ55CXXYofk4tFnIgVHKy6FZrj_6iXHtyCQ2No4
1790194325543092	continuum-dev	itc:v3:AWKSTzM5JJnJPkQAAAAAQar23VW6voAAAAEy4BM		item.comment	bn-36wy3	{"body":"Lead: adversarial finding 4 was declined, and the lead agrees. End-only faults can go away if the journal continues, so Inconclusive is the honest verdict for a truncation, and it is never Conforms. Finding 7 (quadratic scans) is a follow-up bone."}	blake3:0XP02YOf7MU3MDpbXauvh-Kius2RodQ1dgBWSuNIaJw
1790194325723936	continuum-dev	itc:v3:AWKSTzM5JJnJPkQAAAAAQar23VW6voAAAAEy4RM		item.create	bn-15t6z	{"description":"bn-36wy3's adversarial review found that check_none_held, armed_for and the channel scan run over all state on each single-task cancel, so cost grows quadratically with journal length (66 ms at 40k events). Some of these scans predate the bone. Deliver: per-task indexes of open obligations, armed timers and held channel endpoints, maintained incrementally, so each check is O(1) or O(log n). Add an operation-counted regression: work grows linearly as the journal doubles. Untrusted journals reach the lift, so this is a resource bound.","kind":"task","labels":["phase-b","req:phase-b","req:pr-14"],"title":"PR-14 lift: per-task indexes to remove quadratic scans on single-task cancel (bn-36wy3 adversarial finding 7)"}	blake3:7ZCLtVc79G6SrzpJlErzeHqSQRcj4IoPqB4Vo6tgjmk
