1790197495078411	continuum-dev	itc:v3:AWKSTzM5JJnJPkQAAAAAQar23VW6voAAAAEy7RM		item.comment	bn-36wy3	{"body":"cr-3pu5cu round 5 fixed in c03ad5f + 9bbdbf2. HIGH: a deadline's own cancellation now holds every family (check_own_cancel_admits before each family lift): only its phases, its cleanup after ack and before cancelled, and its own cancel. A7 model has the same rule separately. New test: 23 forged events, 974 journals over 32 projections (412 conformed before). MEDIUM: every deadline log lifts under all 32 dropped subsets (242,304). The binding-run test is a stated sample (1,092 logs x 32 = 34,944 runs) and byte-equal to the filtered journal. Full cross-product about 160 s debug, so sampled. Pre-review pass fixed: cleanup implies ack without phases, own work past a deadline refused in every family, repeated region cancel refused. Deferred: work between a region request and ack (lift admits per c53 item 1, A7 refuses; older than this branch), Leaked holder/end check (older than this branch). just check: all pass except lead-owned security-review-present."}	blake3:M9IhzMsKHJQ8XjB3lYZY2t5qGKkkv6Cm3PSNXC4GBis
1790197535037782	continuum-dev	itc:v3:AWKSTzM5JJnJPkQAAAAAQar23VW6voAAAAEy7hM		item.create	bn-28hup	{"description":"Found by the bn-36wy3 round-6 adversarial pass. The lift admits some of a task's work between a region cancel request and that task's acknowledgement, and the A7 model refuses it. The lift matches RFC 0026 c53 item 1, but is inconsistent with itself: timer scheduling is refused and effect reserve is admitted. Choose one rule from docs/02 §7 and RFC 0026. Write it as an RFC correction. Make the lift and the A7 model agree, then re-run the A7 sweep with zero disagreement.","kind":"task","labels":["phase-b","req:pr-14","risk:high","invariant"],"title":"PR-14 lift: one rule for work between a region cancel request and the task's acknowledgement (lift vs A7 divergence)"}	blake3:_EpJluiTLTDVxsLe4hncbCbOuKMWulL0p9z5-AmftWE
