1790202232530344	continuum-dev	itc:v3:AWKSTzM5JJnJPkQAAAAAQar23VW6voAAAAEygRQ		item.comment	bn-36wy3	{"body":"cr-3pu5cu round 8 fixed in 2c23185. (1) A deadline must be the event right after its task's spawn (DeadlineNotAtSpawn), in the lift and the A7 model. The model generator offers it only there. Added a 24th model mutant and a test. The rule is decidable in every projection, because the spawn is lifecycle and projections only drop events. (2) Journal encoding is now v2. The writer emits v2 and the reader reads v1 and v2 with per-version grammar. A v2 tag labelled v1 is TagNotInVersion, and an unknown version is UnsupportedVersion. The A7 reader does the same. The v1 golden still decodes. The version is an encoding contract (schema_epoch sense), not a semantic epoch. v1 journals are Preserved and the blast radius is empty. This is recorded in journal.rs, RFC c53 and the GOV migration note. just check: all pass except the lead-owned security-review-present."}	blake3:Nn37To49Ryg-Wxp9nhRr5UW6pNp-gnGCcMLWzITxegQ
1790203534769381	continuum-dev	itc:v3:AWKSTzM5JJnJPkQAAAAAQar23VW6voAAAAEyghQ		item.comment	bn-23hzh	{"body":"Part C done: commit 624d58e. Option, tuple, Set, and Map state lower to flat slots (x[k], x{u}, x?, x!, x.i). Init takes canonical candidates only, and writes are whole-layout. Keys are static, with the new refusals dynamic_key, value_outside_bound, dynamic_value, duplicate_key, and undefined_read (init). Map reads give the predicates A#defined and I#defined. The register lowers to 14 slots and 50 actions, and tests/register.rs matches it against a hand-written simulation: states, transitions, verdicts, and undefined reads (Nodes without c), plus a mutant. tests/collections.rs checks invariants and actions against an oracle on all 30,720 canonical states. The adversarial pass found 5 issues (3 confirmed): all 5 fixed, with regressions. It also fixed a bn-10j7z plan under-prediction. Sites now spend exactly their prediction. just check: green except security-review-present (lead-owned); dossier, lean, and test-policy pass separately."}	blake3:MFb95nKYY30kcGiNxu6fZY_fBHndcE0ZChqJJ3L4No4
