1790205787220973	continuum-dev	itc:v3:AWKSTzM5JJnJPkQAAAAAQar23VW6voAAAAEyqRQ		item.comment	bn-2npu	{"body":"cr-10mg1y fixes at e872f30. (1) Fair-SCC exclusion: reachability stops at goal states, so dead ends and fair cycles refute eventually-goal only before any goal visit; this also fixes the pre-existing false rejection of post-goal fair cycles. Recurrence docs removed. Tests cover all five ruled cases for kernel verdict and daemon CertificateRejected class, plus a goal-stopped differential. bn-2mm0q (recurrence question) is resolved by the lead ruling: the property is eventually-reached. (2) TCB-01 is id-based (duplicate names, non-member same-name packages, renamed deps fail with witness); C023 graph reader gained package-identity, c023.json regenerated. (3) TCB-02 is a fail-closed public-API inventory (516 items, tools/tcb-audit/public-api.txt), second line behind the Rust entry-point tests; 4 compiling fixtures fail it. Lane: 24/25 checker mutants killed, producer 4 caught/7 missed/1 refused; C018 stays TARGET. just check: all green except lead-owned security-review-present, kernel-reviewers-present, T09 review gates."}	blake3:55kVt0FcErxBpGWvSiQ_zxNqpk5eeZ2_xOy19jb14VU
1790206403232502	continuum-dev	itc:v3:AWKSTzM5JJnJPkQAAAAAQar23VW6voAAAAEyqhQ		item.comment	bn-3glnv	{"body":"cr-2unxyh HIGH (CWE-345) fixed at 7b340d0. Import and export now refuse an in_ or inb_ that names byte-different content with PublicationAborted, not retryable, before any fact, contract or bundle changes. intent.accept compares the bundle's contract bytes with the local contract exactly (ACI). evidence.link refuses a receipt-node identity that names another receipt, before it signs. A colliding signer handle is withdrawn. Every collision is counted, with no content logged. There are 4 injected-collision tests, and mutants of the guards fail them. just check: only the lead-owned security-review-present failure."}	blake3:aMOWc_yqrx6vp_RftaaVxOLIcBlx4fyUmICxthCzFBE
1790207124934558	continuum-dev	itc:v3:AWKSTzM5JJnJPkQAAAAAQar23VW6voAAAAEyqxQ		item.comment	bn-2npu	{"body":"cr-10mg1y round 2 fixed. TCB-02 now closes verdict types over all aliases (private, associated, use-as renames) to a fixed point, checks associated types and trait-impl methods, and fails closed on unresolvable projections. Each of 8 compiling fixtures (incl. two-hop, reverse-order multi-hop, private alias, associated Output, re-exported alias) carries its own inventory lines and must show its semantic diagnostic; inventory drift fails the self-test. Evidence reports the closure next to every entry point. Lane rerun unchanged: 24/25 checker kills; producer 4/7/1. just check green except lead-owned security-review-present, kernel-reviewers-present, T09 review gates."}	blake3:Qbd2Qr-poDM4i_dBywCWy4h36L0UScslQ951xdqVgks
1790207241448359	continuum-dev	itc:v3:AWKSTzM5JJnJPkQAAAAAQar23VW6voAAAAEyrBQ		item.comment	bn-28hup	{"body":"Done in ws bn-28hup, commit bf46fd2. Rule (RFC 0026 correction 55): a task that a cancellation request reached takes no step before it acknowledges. That covers its own work in every family, receipts, and (with phases) its aborted discharge, leak or receiver drop. The rule holds under all 32 projections. It is applied in the lift (CancellationFault::BeforeAcknowledgement) and separately in the A7 model (Fault::Unobserved). It narrows the calculus, which is unchanged; the narrowing is named in pr14_impl01 (532 interleavings). New tests: a_requested_task_acknowledges_before_it_does_anything (512 controls, 704 refused, 24 admitted) and every_family_is_held_to_the_acknowledgement (576). 3 new mutants (27 total). The A7 sweep has 0 disagreements. Pre-review pass: timer fire in the window added, terminal-task fault misattribution fixed, counts pinned. just check: pass."}	blake3:TQdHNxcT0kpDehdJ829f0n5LEnqWuRvUAJ9Y_vzwrWA
