1790209744871160	continuum-dev	itc:v3:AWKSTzM5JJnJPkQAAAAAQar23VW6voAAAAEywhQ		item.comment	bn-2npu	{"body":"cr-10mg1y round 4 fixed. (1) Every fn token in the checking base must parse (raw idents, qualified paths); unparsable fails. Rust authority tests walk src/, fail on unexpected files, and catch raw idents/qualified/split signatures. (2) KCOV-07 covers continuum-certificate and bans include_str!/include_bytes! and mod-without-file; TCB-02 relays it; digest covers every file under the 5 crates plus Cargo.toml, Cargo.lock, rust-toolchain.toml. (3) TCB-05 validates the whole record (controls, fixture compiles, rows, summary, measurements, producer fields) and --evidence writes atomically only on success. Note: producer fields are now strict, so an edit to engine-reference or model-core src needs a lane rerun. 16 TCB-02 fixtures compile; lane 24/25, producer 4/7/1. just check green except lead-owned security-review-present, kernel-reviewers-present, T09 review gates."}	blake3:WzL5UitqrRIgDqRq2goLlEDunVXYHqQPBnQBLRMjnns
1790209985433897	continuum-dev	itc:v3:AWKSTzM5JJnJPkQAAAAAQar23VW6voAAAAEywxQ		item.comment	bn-3glnv	{"body":"cr-2unxyh round 2 fixed at 8875784. The bundle now carries key-attested SignerLinks and no audit log. A rotation is signed by both keys; a compromise revocation is signed by the revoked key. They are adopted only after the bundle signature and every link authenticate, only on the concerned keys' own word, and never for a loss recovery. Known and unseen keys are treated alike, and adoption is bounded by the pinned set. A retiring key pre-signs its revocation, then is wiped. An active held key always keeps room for its revocation; a replacement is refused only if it could not be revoked in turn, and a loss recovery falls back to a plain revoke. There are 2 fresh-opus adversarial passes; the last found no code blocker. Residual, documented in ADR-0054: links, pre-signed revocations and own-key identity are not persisted across restart. Follow-up bone needed; this also absorbs bn-g7f1h. just check: only the lead-owned security-review-present failure."}	blake3:QE4hmgGUqchhm6M0V-mFYH_L-34MgMY4nHEDuqSWxAg
1790210012510276	continuum-dev	itc:v3:AWKSTzM5JJnJPkQAAAAAQar23VW6voAAAAEyxBQ		item.comment	bn-18w74	{"body":"Scope added by bn-3glnv round 2: persist signer links (own and adopted), pre-signed revocations and the own-key set with the registry. Record own keys apart from the registry's signers. Today install treats every registry signer as the daemon's own (an ADR-0054 residual)."}	blake3:QX6TpScwEsRb8olgeXMEbcBzfLp7sVWBHlQxPYfUErk
1790210012550805	continuum-dev	itc:v3:AWKSTzM5JJnJPkQAAAAAQar23VW6voAAAAEyxRQ		item.comment	bn-3glnv	{"body":"Lead: I accept 8875784. Revoking an active held key always succeeds, and only a replacement that could not itself be revoked is refused (fail-safe). The persistence residual is folded into bn-18w74. Codex round 3 is retargeted."}	blake3:e3OU01ohCQ5dmKVyYmXg0ai6wHvLQ0NJaheEEXPi5Z8
