1790211691049153	continuum-dev	itc:v3:AWKSTzM5JJnJPkQAAAAAQar23VW6voAAAAEyxxQ		item.comment	bn-2npu	{"body":"cr-3i3rst round 5 fixed. The audit now runs cargo check --locked for the 5 checking crates and reads rustc's dep-info: compiled files must equal scanned files (either direction fails; missing/stale dep-info or a failed build fails closed), and compiled inputs join the TCB-05 digest. cfg_attr naming path is banned in KCOV-07 (all 5 crates) and TCB-02. New compiling cfg_attr-redirect fixture (dummy src/m.rs present): lexical ban fires in self-test, dep-info rule fires in the lane; self-test shows a changed redirect target fails TCB-05. Real tree: dep-info equals scan set. Lane 24/25; producer 4/7/1; 17 fixtures compile. just check green except lead-owned security-review-present, kernel-reviewers-present, T09 review gates."}	blake3:nBi8dPC9S-38uNTa2v4n1ILz_HQqxlaWQ5Z2ymWxELw
1790211954809931	continuum-dev	itc:v3:AWKSTzM5JJnJPkQAAAAAQar23VW6voAAAAEyyBQ		item.comment	bn-eaxx0	{"body":"Fixed in 16945d7. obligation.rs finish() typed a finalized-not-settled region Violates(Unsettled) even for an ordinary truncation. Now Inconclusive(InsufficientTelemetry), unless this family's own ledger for the region already shows an open or leaked obligation, in which case it stays Violates(UnbalancedAtClose) exactly as a disagreeing settle event would. Pre-review adversarial pass found the naive unconditional-Incomplete fix reopened a real hole (ordinary Complete/Fail does not check held obligations, so a forged journal could finalize a region over one and never report it); fixed by reading region_balance at finish, same as a real settle is held to. LedgerFault::Unsettled removed. Sweeps in a7_primitive_conformance.rs and pr14_deadline_cancellation.rs now assert Inconclusive specifically for every finalize-not-settled prefix (6,043 cases in the A7 corpus). Two new regression tests: a_journal_cut_between_finalize_and_settle_is_inconclusive and a_finalized_region_with_an_open_obligation_and_no_settle_is_unbalanced_not_inconclusive, both verified to fail against the wrong fix. Mutant 7 in pr14_impl04_obligations.rs updated to expect Inconclusive. RFC 0026 correction 56 added. A7 model needed no change (its own end check already had the same rule; agreement is boolean accept/reject only). just check: pass."}	blake3:wz5Q7d6RKfZqTDg9dRYZvsMVHOgLo47Skmr8HibOdWg
