1790212249274338	continuum-dev	itc:v3:AWKSTzM5JJnJPkQAAAAAQar23VW6voAAAAEyyhQ		item.comment	bn-3jz	{"body":"Done: commit 4c564b0. tests/pr15a_identity.rs pins the replicated register: a hand-built ModelBuilder twin from RFC 0003 and the register's own text (no lowering internals called) has one identity with the CML lowering under the schema example run config, both pinned to a committed golden hex, plus three anti-vacuity mutants (guard, fairness scope, slot bound). Die Hard's existing independent differential (tests/diehard_differential.rs, bn-ybq oracle) gets the same golden-hex pin. No other Wave 0 fixture lowers yet (CoffeeCan, TowerOfHanoi, TransitiveClosure, SyntaxCoverage all refuse, unconfigured or configured); continuum-corpus is still a stub. START_HERE_IMPLEMENTATION.md's PR 15a exit and its 'enough surface' bullet are annotated delivered; just traceability regenerated. just check: green (fmt, clippy, full workspace tests, crate boundaries, dossier, lean, GOV4 obligations, test-policy)."}	blake3:Cb-8FLnXM0-jdr-HGfcOwhKgpYDvEejhMIULsMpWqxs
