1790212957183351	continuum-dev	itc:v3:AWKSTzM5JJnJPkQAAAAAQar23VW6voAAAAEyzBQ		item.comment	bn-2npu	{"body":"cr-3i3rst round 6 fixed. TCB-02 and all five Rust authority tests now refuse any public static, const (incl. associated), alias, struct/tuple field or enum variant field whose type names Fn/FnMut/FnOnce/fn(/dyn/impl or a verdict-closure type ('public value the scan cannot prove wire-only'), and any public trait method returning a verdict. Scope note: the verdict enums' own variants (Verdict::Verified(CheckedClaim), Outcome::Checked(KernelVerdict), KernelVerdict::Core(..)) would trip the literal rule; they are allowed to hold verdict types but not callables. Otherwise the real base trips nothing. Five compiling fixtures each give their exact diagnostic and fail the core authority test in the lane. Lane 24/25; producer 4/7/1; 22 fixtures. just check green except lead-owned security-review-present, kernel-reviewers-present, T09 review gates."}	blake3:N0fiJEqTVNx4Fznu-l4x4lrjzXAfnO0kqs54IGmVKkc
