1790217294345122	continuum-dev	itc:v3:AWKSTzM5JJnJPkQAAAAAQar23VW6voAAAAEyghU		item.comment	bn-31ie2	{"body":"Reconciled the normative spec surface (RFC 0031/0032/0038, docs/11, docs/41)\nagainst Phase B code. Commit 1ae7e376 (docs-only).\n\nReconciliation table:\n\n| Doc/section | Disagreement | Resolution |\n|---|---|---|\n| docs/11 (whole doc) | Never touched since initial dossier authoring (86ed17ef); predates all of RFC 0003's corrections 1-5 and every landed CLI/protocol/syntax PR | Added a Status/normative-source banner: RFC 0003 governs CML semantics, RFC 0026 IDL + continuum-cli govern wire/CLI; docs/11 corrected inline |\n| docs/11 §3 type universe | No mention of finiteness/bounds; silent on which types are exhaustively checkable | Added correction-4 paragraph: Bool/sort/enum/bounded Nat-Int/Option/tuple/Set/Map are finite; sequences/strings/records/functions are not |\n| docs/11 §4 actions | Frame-rule sentence present but uncited | Added pointer to RFC 0003 \"Relational actions\" (correction 2, bn-2ouro) as the precise implemented rule |\n| docs/11 §5 nondeterminism | `Set<Node>` angle-bracket syntax does not match implemented `Name[T,...]` application syntax; `choose` shown as usable | Fixed to `Set[Node]`; noted `choose` parses but elaboration refuses it (`cml.unsupported.choose`) |\n| docs/11 §6 modules/views | `Map<Key,Value>` wrong bracket syntax; `view`/`map`/`visible action` presented as available | Fixed brackets; noted no `view` keyword exists in `continuum-cml-syntax` — design sketch only |\n| docs/11 §7 property syntax | `transition invariant`, `assuming`, `hyperproperty` shown as syntax | Noted only `invariant`/`always`/`eventually` are lexed; the rest is unimplemented |\n| docs/11 §8 static analyses | \"totality/termination\" listed as an open analysis | Noted it is RFC 0003's landed normative rule (bn-36x3b), not open |\n| docs/11 §9 CLI | `continuum check model.ctm` etc. does not exist; real CLI is handle/wire-based | Replaced with the actual 8-noun `continuum-cli` surface (snapshot/check/explain/context/task/debug/repair/evidence); old sketch kept as labeled long-term direction |\n| docs/11 §13 agent protocol | Ten illustrative op names (`model.inspect`, `trace.slice`, ...) are not on the wire | Pointed at the real `continuumd-native-protocol.idl` (RFC 0026, 70+ ops/19 namespaces) and named the closest landed analogues |\n| RFC 0031 | Spot-checked assurance movement, correction 20 (`change_policy.rs::verdict`), fairness/observers/properties classifiers | Matches landed code by file and symbol; no new divergence |\n| RFC 0032 | Spot-checked gate profiles, wire structs (`continuumd::protocol::operations::repair`) | Matches; `continuum-repair` itself is still a PR-20 stub, but RFC says \"Draft for implementation\" and claims nothing built — not a disagreement, just a build-status note |\n| RFC 0038 | Spot-checked D1-D4 (`CheckTargetRule`), P1-P7 (`derivation.rs`), W1-W12/V1-V6 (`whiteboard.rs`, `view.rs`) | Matches; already self-corrected with bone-cited history |\n| docs/41 | Already regenerated around RFC 0032 (SD-10, bn-7kj) and schema-swept (bn-1lfek) | No change needed; confirmed non-normative banner and content still agree with RFC 0032 |\n\nNo divergence required weakening a requirement or changing an intent/claim\nmeaning; none needed the spec-debt ledger (all resolved by prose correction).\n\nCode follow-ups for the lead (not fixed here, per instructions):\n- None required by a code/RFC mismatch. The only build-status gap found is\n  `crates/continuum-repair/src/lib.rs` still being the PR-20 scaffold stub —\n  expected per plan §8's phasing, not a spec violation.\n\n`just traceability` (mechanical regen, +1 bone in registry, unrelated to\nthis change) and `just dossier` both pass (status: pass). `cd $WS &&\nTMPDIR=$WS/target/tmp CARGO_BUILD_JOBS=8 just check` exits 0. HEAD:\n1ae7e3766950198757ea64cc05435b0b0bb29127.\n\nBone left open per instructions — spans all of Phase B."}	blake3:E0WKstj5DDgvfPwur-X-RkzqK5o8dNGZz7YLmgUsOG8
