1790218653739785	continuum-dev	itc:v3:AWKSTzM5JJnJPkQAAAAAQar23VW6voAAAAEyihU		item.comment	bn-1nmq	{"body":"cr-3rqxh8 addressed, HEAD d2672c3d (not merged). parser.rs ty_inner now measures an arrow's left side with the high-water mark and charges it one level when the arrow arrives: Tn = Set[Tn-1] -> Nat (T63 was a 127-deep tree accepted at MAX_NESTING) is refused at the arrow; every accepted type tree is <= MAX_NESTING. Audit: only binary chains, postfix chains, and the arrow re-attach a parsed subtree; all three now bounded by real depth. Oracle: cml_fuzz/depth.rs walks every expression and type root (exhaustive field patterns); new DeepType mutant arms it; new nested-function-type mutation. Tests: errors.rs adversarial_function_types_cannot_stack_past_the_bound, cml_fuzz.rs the_function_type_boundary_holds_on_the_probe_stack (T31/T32/T62/T63/T64 on the 1 MiB probe stack, all 4 targets); both and the gate campaign fail on the pre-fix parser. just check: governance fails only on lead-owned security-review-present (T09 review gates); dossier fails only on PLAN_BONE_TRACEABILITY staleness (lead-owned, not regenerated); lean, test-policy, and the other governance steps pass."}	blake3:V-uoCWjEvkdI7gLprCxTTRwYmluMmt5l0NV2YL0NVkQ
1790218738956954	continuum-dev	itc:v3:AWKSTzM5JJnJPkQAAAAAQar23VW6voAAAAEyixU		item.comment	bn-2rsp	{"body":"IMPL-02 delivered in WS bn-2rsp (HEAD 3e93b2a3). Model notes/plan/examples/durable_register.ctm plus run config: storage-level voting register, Reserve/Submit/Sync/Abort/Lose/Ack. Engine establishes Agreement, AckedIsDurable, OneValuePerSlot at claim-A scope (3 nodes, 2 values, 2 epochs, 61,504 states). Crash is uncounted there. A counted crash is InitDomainTooLarge at that scope. Atomic crashes <=2 reach exactly the established set. Crash adds no reachable state, only transitions. The claim-A lowering needs an explicit work budget of 2^34. Tests: crates/continuum-cml-elab/tests/pr16_impl02_durable_register.rs, 20 tests: prose-slot differential, step correspondence onto the lowered abstract register, durability step check, 6 seeded bugs, 5 boundaries. Golden has 14 artifact IDs pr16-impl02-*. No src change, no new dependency. just check: pass, exit 0."}	blake3:b3c8liQPwHwnlbCxUXSWVubnokBLEbDPFdrlvP9ekkg
1790218795147219	continuum-dev	itc:v3:AWKSTzM5JJnJPkQAAAAAQar23VW6voAAAAEyjBU		item.comment	bn-rkrt7	{"body":"Done: commit 730a7d6 (workspace bn-rkrt7). fairness_dimension() in crates/continuumd/src/daemon/verification.rs now reads the task's registered Model instead of hardcoding unsupported(no-fairness-model). This engine binds obligations() to invariants only (Fragment::Temporal stays unsupported), so it never calls continuum_engine_reference::liveness, fairness's one consumer; the dimension therefore stays unsupported, never produced, so no result overstates fairness the engine used. The reason token now distinguishes the two true cases: no Model or an empty Model::fairness() keeps no-fairness-model; a Model with a declared assumption reports the new token fairness-declared-unused, naming the fact without interpolating strength or scope (rule envelope.no_prose). This fills the existing free-string UnsupportedDimension.reason field; no IDL or schema change, following the crate's own precedent for situation-specific reason tokens (no-fairness-obligation, no-observer-projection in evidence.rs). 4 new unit tests in verification.rs::tests cover a model with fairness, a model without, no model, and never-produced. just check: green (fmt, clippy, workspace tests, dossier validator, lean, test-policy)."}	blake3:sacEHMV8TTlPLN-BJLVs8_bO9KFT6Fz1e1ENWC71BJQ
