1790219731672998	continuum-dev	itc:v3:AWKSTzM5JJnJPkQAAAAAQar23VW6voAAAAEyoRU		item.comment	bn-10mth	{"body":"Fixed at 817c1768 (ws bn-10mth). intent.lock starts only from an accepted lineage head that carries its acceptance block, and refuses a successor the registry already holds. intent.accept decides a revision before protection: the predecessor must be the accepted head, and no field that the predecessor protects moves (the same stand-in that import uses). Accepting a revision supersedes the head on either path. RFC 0037 correction 22 records this. 8 new daemon_operations tests. The g1_03 pin moved intent.lock to answer-distinguished (13/18). The daemon_signing lineage tests were reworked. 7 guard-removal mutants each fail a test. just check exit 0. No GOV-4 record: check_obligations reports no semantic change."}	blake3:NKqh2b5alH_USX-wWfpWHjT9dDOaUwxMT16LcAVtmvQ
