1790224046506699	continuum-dev	itc:v3:AWKSTzM5JJnJPkQAAAAAQar23VW6voAAAAEyvRU		item.comment	bn-1uspo	{"body":"Delivered at 324946ea: research/35 gains an eleventh red-team class, ForgedSigningLineage (Vector::RedTeam), with its ratified 3-case floor in continuum-security/src/injection.rs, planted on intent.accept/evidence.link/task.resume (protocol-version-agnostic Case, so the wire-shaped 3.2 corpus carries the floor while the signing wire needs 3.8). daemon_signing.rs gains every_signing_wire_operation_refuses_or_answers_typed_for_an_unprivileged_reader and the_signing_wires_refusal_does_not_move_with_a_hostile_corpus_payload, driving signing.mint/rotate/revoke/sign_pack/registry/verify and intent.import_bundle directly at 3.8 against the real daemon with the corpus's own payloads: typed CapabilityDenied (or a typed inert answer for the two reads) and an unmoved registry, asserted every time. The other 4 named attack surfaces (rotation cycles/tails, oversize frames and link lists, colliding identities, fabricated acceptance-chain tokens, key material never echoed) are already discharged by real, reviewed daemon_signing.rs tests from bn-3glnv (cross-referenced by name in the new section's doc comment) rather than duplicated as new corpus cases, so the corpus stays exactly the ratified taxonomy (gate_g2_07_acceptance.rs pins CASES.len() == floor, no surplus). No defects found. Updated: plan.md/research/35.md/plan.typ ratified-gate quote (ten->eleven classes, 45->48 cases), dependency-rationale.toml, TEST-9-07 absence text + regenerated evidence, and every downstream pin in gate_g1/g2_07_acceptance.rs and inv015_agent_least_authority_evidence.rs. just traceability and just dossier both pass. just check: green (fmt, clippy, full workspace test, boundaries, covenant, governance, dossier, lean, test-policy). No src/ behaviour changed. Follow-up (not filed, for the lead): the six signing-wire operations still run through SIGNING_WIRE_PROBES in g2_injection_corpus_evidence.rs rather than as real corpus Cases, because Case is deliberately protocol-version-agnostic and that file's shared runner fixes protocol 3.2 for the whole corpus in one pass; closing it needs the runner to learn a per-case protocol floor."}	blake3:EDQWpb0W6uY0X30vlx5Sikc_DePoDUP78Pf7XTEf4-A
