1790224336122127	continuum-dev	itc:v3:AWKSTzM5JJnJPkQAAAAAQar23VW6voAAAAEywRU		item.comment	bn-5p7c1	{"body":"continuum-cml-elab::Unsupported gains ALL, [Unsupported;5], compile-time pinned to each variant: private ordinal() matches with no wildcard arm, and each arm carries a const assertion (const _: () = assert!(matches!(Unsupported::ALL[I], Variant))) evaluated while the crate builds regardless of whether ordinal is called, so an omitted variant, a reused index, or an index past ALL's length fails the build. An adversarial opus review first found the naive pigeonhole-only version (sorted ordinals of ALL against 0..len()) could not detect an omitted or index-reused variant; verified the gap and the fix empirically with standalone rustc scratch files before landing it. cml_laws.rs's law (c) semantic half (bn-1nmq) now iterates Unsupported::ALL instead of a hand-kept ELAB_UNSUPPORTED copy. Also fixed: a vacuous 'metamorphic' test that only proved sort_unstable is order-independent (deleted, replaced with a documented relation note on the real boundary-splicing test), and an overclaiming differential test name/doc (renamed to state only what it checks: nonempty and code-disjoint). GOV §4 record: tools/governance/reviews/bn-5p7c1.toml (no security table). HEAD 0f38ca0. just check: only failure is the lead-owned security-review-present gate; fmt, clippy, cargo test --workspace, boundaries, covenant, governance (all but that one line), dossier, lean, and test-policy all pass."}	blake3:fwS9Ot16ln7YUrJNMOYW90jXkPEwqnqc9JDxvHirfKo
