1790224795926636	continuum-dev	itc:v3:AWKSTzM5JJnJPkQAAAAAQar23VW6voAAAAEywxU		item.comment	bn-1mgcv	{"body":"Fixed at 3f65b2bb (ws bn-1mgcv). workspace.create uses accepted_head, so a superseded record, accepted with no block, or accepted naming a successor gives AcceptanceChainInvalid and creates nothing. A lock successor's acceptance names the lock: admitted actor, daemon time, and the lock's audit record. It signs its own A1 chain (successor, base = predecessor) when the daemon signs acceptances; otherwise it records 'unsigned' with no chain. A lock with no clock or with a revoked key gives UnsupportedSemanticFeature and changes nothing. A peer's CI check now verifies the lock actor and refuses the original acceptor. BundleRecord::parse refuses a record whose status and superseded_by disagree. The duplicate FAULTS entry is removed. RFC 0037 correction 23 records this. 9 new tests. 7 mutants each fail a test. Fork residual and unsigned-accept attribution are stated in the RFC. just check exit 0."}	blake3:6WI7UCBo4SmqQr0VzH2P1ziEK_mkwfM9yX0OJdFBGpY
1790225064782765	continuum-dev	itc:v3:AWKSTzM5JJnJPkQAAAAAQar23VW6voAAAAEyxBU		item.comment	bn-3ohe	{"body":"cr-1dl1d7 fixed at 26e31795. (1)+(2): the pack is #![no_std] with extern crate alloc. tests/pr15_no_std_lane.rs cargo-checks a scratch copy in dev and release: the control compiles, and a planted std::net use fails with E0433 on std. The same structure rules are enforced in the lane, in the INV-015 audit and in gov4_pack_kernel.py: #![no_std] first; no cfg, cfg_attr, macro_rules, include, path, asm or raw token; the only extern crate is alloc; no build.rs; manifest has only [package] and [lints] workspace=true. The GOV-4-13 waiver also needs a live profile test that does assert_eq!(<P>.host, HostQualification::None), every declared host must be None, and a live lane test (no should_panic/cfg/ignore). 55 fixtures; self-test passes. The substring scan is gone. (3): max_retained_bytes bounds the canonical journal size and is precharged in admit; replay is lazy; encode writes exactly retained bytes; boundary tests added. Fresh opus pass: 10 findings, all fixed. Gate by recipe: all exit 0 except governance, which fails only on the lead-owned GOV-4-15 independence-review finding; T09 fails on the same finding."}	blake3:F0P8vVLr8CeTSjpH1f1fM1r4DWdBGl3aI2UVg26UVKc
1790225366857849	continuum-dev	itc:v3:AWKSTzM5JJnJPkQAAAAAQar23VW6voAAAAEyxRU		item.create	bn-2jhx4	{"description":"bn-1mgcv, RFC 0037 correction 23 residual: workspace.fork keeps a base bound to a superseded intent, so new work can continue under a contract that no longer governs. The fork errors clause declares no code that could refuse it. Add AcceptanceChainInvalid, or a fitting code, to the fork clause in the IDL. This is an IDL change, so check whether it needs a protocol minor bump and bring that to the lead. Refuse fork of a non-head base.","kind":"task","labels":["phase-b","req:phase-b","security","risk:high"],"title":"workspace.fork keeps a base bound to a superseded intent; add a typed refusal (IDL change) (bn-1mgcv follow-up)"}	blake3:7Cdy4jCzWPwsxrBz_Rv6BHaAd3B6hQY_LSxSdyyL7OU
