1790225826741112	continuum-dev	itc:v3:AWKSTzM5JJnJPkQAAAAAQar23VW6voAAAAEyyxU		item.comment	bn-1uspo	{"body":"cr-21ahx9 addressed at 344f37b5. HIGH: forged-signing-lineage/isolation-escape used task.resume, but Continuation/Budget are fully typed (no string field anywhere in daemon/task.rs's Continuation or continuum-model-core's State), so the shared runner's ContinuationHandle::new(payload) fallback silently substituted a fixed nonexistent handle and the case never carried its payload. Moved it to observe.ingest (instrumentation_profile, against the fixture's real staged receipt) which does carry the payload for real; only the carrying/inert split in gate_g2_07_acceptance.rs needed re-deriving (27/10 -> 28/9), everything else was unaffected. Checked the same fallback against every other task.resume isolation-escape case: stale-snapshot-substitution/isolation-escape (injection.rs:573) and isolation/hard-kill (injection.rs:953) are equally vacuous by the identical mechanism (g2_injection_corpus_evidence.rs:681-687), both predating bn-1uspo (bn-ugee0/bn-2a7q9-era). Flagging both rather than fixing: task.resume has no string field to carry a payload through at all, so a real fix needs a genuinely hostile stored continuation (tampered pinned epochs or foreign task ownership), which touches already-shipped, already-reviewed corpus content outside this bone's scope. MEDIUM: the_signing_wires_refusal_does_not_move_with_a_hostile_corpus_payload now separates the payload-free group (signing.mint/rotate/revoke, checked once each for CapabilityDenied + unmoved registry, explicitly not counted as a differential) from the three real carriers (sign_pack, verify, import_bundle); signing.verify's hostile-vs-benign check now compares the whole typed SigningVerifyResponse (outcome, signer, successor), not just the error code, which was None either way and could have hidden a content-sensitive difference. just check: green in the foreground (fmt, clippy, full workspace test, boundaries, covenant, governance, dossier, lean, test-policy). No src/ changed. HEAD: 344f37b5376532fac788df4b78e1e148069eec50."}	blake3:oXLFiz3o0Yx_eKMtmv4O6mdPFc5ktEefJeR5BoPrhR4
1790225873171305	continuum-dev	itc:v3:AWKSTzM5JJnJPkQAAAAAQar23VW6voAAAAEyzBU		item.create	bn-2zccj	{"description":"Found by bn-1uspo (Codex cr-21ahx9). task.resume carries no string field: Continuation and Budget are fully typed. So the shared runner in g2_injection_corpus_evidence.rs:681-687 parses the payload as a ContinuationHandle and, when that fails, silently substitutes a fixed nonexistent handle. stale-snapshot-substitution/isolation-escape (injection.rs:573) and isolation/hard-kill (injection.rs:953) are therefore vacuous, yet they count toward the gate floor. Fix: give each case a real carrier, such as a hostile STORED continuation (tampered pinned epochs, or foreign task ownership, through TaskTable::park) or an operation that carries the text. Make the runner fail loudly and never substitute. Re-derive the gate_g2_07 counts. Check whether the plan §24.5 gate evidence overstated and, if so, correct the prose.","kind":"task","labels":["phase-b","req:phase-b","security","risk:high"],"title":"research/35 corpus: two isolation-escape cases on task.resume are vacuous (payload never carried); fix the carriers and make the runner fail loudly"}	blake3:wcWReAG6wqXz9osItwYyM6WOL2nBlf8382J0zo4N6G8
