1790228951426923	continuum-dev	itc:v3:AWKSTzM5JJnJPkQAAAAAQar23VW6voAAAAEy4BU		item.comment	bn-3mmf	{"body":"continuum-effects-process: process/crash-restart-v0 0.1.0 profile (11 rows: 6 modelled, 3 unsupported with Unsupported refusals, 2 with no step) and Lab handler over explicit Begin/Complete/Delay/Crash/Restart choice logs. A crash is fail-stop. Tickets of the crashed incarnation stay pending, and a late completion is Fenced (M08). Restart epochs strictly increase (M03). The COMPOSITION table states what a crash does to network envelopes, storage and runtime state. no_std with the network pack's compiler lane. 25 tests: exhaustive differential vs an independent model (3,733 states, 14 model mutants caught), 2,100-log determinism, replay, step-boundary truncation, crash-window splices (6,000 windows, 3,629 runs, 1,551 fenced completions), pinned journal hex and profile fingerprint. INV-015: process moved from the scaffold sweep to a 4-leg audit plus a mutant test. Record tools/governance/reviews/bn-3mmf.toml has no independence_review or security table (lead-owned). Fresh opus pre-review: 8 findings, 7 fixed, 1 accepted (leaked-effects row scoped). just check exit 1: only governance fails, on the lead-owned GOV-4-15 independence-review-present finding (T09 review gates reruns check_obligations). Every other step passes. Commit 5d4f0801."}	blake3:_syzsJkWQJDxNTlZHc1NWueUYvEcbntxIWS00EcAK88
1790228990454107	continuum-dev	itc:v3:AWKSTzM5JJnJPkQAAAAAQar23VW6voAAAAEy4RU		item.create	bn-20d8u	{"description":"bn-3mmf's process profile distinguishes a fail-stop crash (no finalizer or cancellation handler runs, pending completions are fenced by (node, epoch)) from graceful cancellation. The PR-16 register program (bn-131yp, bn-5fpl, bn-28oa) realizes a replica crash as cancellation of the replica's region, so cancellation handlers and aborts run. That is graceful cancellation, and claims about crash behaviour in the IMPL-03/04/05 evidence may overstate fail-stop coverage. Either drive crashes through the process pack's fail-stop semantics, or restate the PR-16 evidence and START_HERE annotations as 'crash modelled as graceful cancellation', and add fail-stop coverage. Check the M07 torn-tail and M02 lost-abort mutants under fail-stop.","kind":"task","labels":["phase-b","req:phase-b","req:pr-16","risk:high","invariant"],"title":"PR-16 register realizes a crash as region cancellation, which is graceful cancellation under process/crash-restart-v0, not fail-stop; reconcile (bn-3mmf finding)"}	blake3:zf-wdgM0ToFEZEPtNQM8_YQXfXJh-MwMg_An_swF6OA
