1790229051256541	continuum-dev	itc:v3:AWKSTzM5JJnJPkQAAAAAQar23VW6voAAAAEy5RU		item.comment	bn-28oa	{"body":"IMPL-05 in WS bn-28oa at HEAD 3d025485, not merged. The mutants are in crates/continuum-asupersync/tests/support/register_mutants.rs. tests/pr16_impl05_mutants.rs holds 15 tests, and the golden has 11 IDs pr16-impl05-mut-00..10-*. Each campaign derives from pr16-correct-baseline: seed 104729, the same groups and log counts, and a digest identity. Detected with replayed witnesses: M01 RuntimeToAbstract plus Agreement through the causal core; M02 RuntimeToAbstract in 24 runs of 4 plans, other runs are typed ReservationDropped refusals; M04 and M07 RuntimeToAbstract; M05 RuntimeToAbstract plus Agreement; M06 Quiescence. Excluded: M03 is typed TaskEnded on every run of every changed plan; M08 has every timer cancelled or fired before the crash, and 0 stale fires. Deferred: M09 to bn-2et/bn-1mm, M10 to bn-voq4. The baseline has 0 findings with the IMPL-04 identity. IMPL-03 and IMPL-04 goldens are unchanged. An adversarial pass found no blocker, and its 6 should-fix items are fixed. Exit annotated in part. just check: exit 0."}	blake3:2eWnf6KZ1YvqvwjE-9MPo_dCXz35ErqHGHxtspA-D_c
1790229083683867	continuum-dev	itc:v3:AWKSTzM5JJnJPkQAAAAAQar23VW6voAAAAEy5hU		item.comment	bn-342ek	{"body":"Fixed at 2166e0d2 (ws bn-342ek). Unsigned local intent.accept -- below 3.8, or with no acceptance-signing key -- now shares intent.accept's signed-path check: accepted_by must be the admitted actor and timestamp this daemon's own clock, else AcceptanceChainInvalid, registry unchanged. No clock reading fails closed as intent.lock does, UnsupportedSemanticFeature. Both local paths call one require_admitted_locally. RFC 0037 correction 23 extended to close its stated residual; the registry schema's audit_record description and the IDL rule intent.bundles prose are corrected (were stale, naming only intent.accept as the acceptance block's producer, when intent.lock also writes one, bn-1mgcv). Prose only, no shape or version change. Tests: an_unsigned_local_acceptance_names_only_the_admitted_principal_at_the_daemons_time (foreign accepted_by, foreign timestamp, control) in daemon_signing.rs; a_local_accept_with_no_clock_reading_is_refused_and_changes_nothing in daemon_operations.rs. A manual mutant removing the unsigned-path check was applied and reverted: both new tests failed against it. Existing fixtures in daemon_operations.rs, daemon_task_operations.rs, and dx12_falsification.rs that drove an unsigned accept through an unclocked daemon or a mismatched caller timestamp are corrected to the honest admission. just check exit 0."}	blake3:87SY0RQLs55amvnE0Y6Y4I6SzU9TX5RttX9eBGgWHlg
