1790229402278608	continuum-dev	itc:v3:AWKSTzM5JJnJPkQAAAAAQar23VW6voAAAAEy7hU		item.comment	bn-18w74	{"body":"Delivered at bc56b190 (not merged). SigningCustodyState + SigningCustody in continuum-evidence; continuumd commits every signing change through the custody before it takes effect (rollback + refuse-all on failure), records own keys apart from registry signers (ADR-0054 residual closed), Builder::launch_signing loads/mints, re-validates (reserve, own keys, link attestation/topology, presigned), sweeps. LocalKeystore: atomic state file + per-key 0600 seeds, O_NOFOLLOW/fstat reads, size bounds, store lock, ancestor-owner and hard-link checks, legacy layout refused. Tests: signing_custody.rs (16), keystore.rs (22). Fresh-opus pass: B1 reserve mismatch + S1-S4 fixed. ADR-0054 revised; GOV record tools/governance/reviews/bn-18w74.toml without security table. just check: only lead-owned security-review-present (T09 review gates) fails; dossier, lean, test-policy pass."}	blake3:H4aiuN1-pFNjUGNN-YtF4Q5u4ECg2w7vant-ESSWDpw
1790229437328897	continuum-dev	itc:v3:AWKSTzM5JJnJPkQAAAAAQar23VW6voAAAAEy7xU		item.create	bn-3snfi	{"description":"bn-18w74 persists signing custody, but held intent bundles and import records are still memory-only. After a restart, intent.accept naming a bundle that was held before the restart fails closed until the bundle is imported again. This is recorded in ADR-0054 and in TEST-9-07's absence text. Persist them with the same custody discipline: atomic writes, descriptor-bound reads, bounded decode, and fail closed on corruption.","kind":"task","labels":["phase-b","req:phase-b","security","risk:high"],"title":"Persist held intent bundles and import records across restart (bn-18w74 follow-up)"}	blake3:BGzO0c8_7UclFwIS10q6zsGZCP_kWGdR_mAT_OZo8vE
