1790268790368177	continuum-dev	itc:v3:AWKSTzM5JJnJPkQAAAAAQar23VW6voAAAAEyhxY		item.create	bn-35cru	{"description":"Found by bn-2zccj (Codex cr-2rgnsb round 2). evidence.verify is declared @mutation @task_starting with authority read. A read-level caller that names an existing observation node makes the daemon re-derive it and write Observed (evidence.rs:1100-1122, 1323-1332). The payload does not cause it (the benign twin does the same), and the value is the checker's. But plan §24.5 requires zero unprivileged evidence-status alterations, and gate_g2_07 now reports that clause REFUTED. Decide whether the design is intended (the checker is the authority, so a reader may request verification), or raise evidence.verify to execute or a node-scoped grant. Changing an operation's authority is an IDL change and needs a protocol decision from the user. If intended, amend the §24.5 gate interpretation through a ratified revision, which is also a user decision.","kind":"task","labels":["phase-b","req:phase-b","security","risk:high"],"title":"evidence.verify is a @mutation at authority read: any reader can trigger a lasting BOTTOM→Observed promotion on any node it can name (research/35 gate clause refuted)"}	blake3:h5dvvRJYdpv_9ynfLtw_YneHTgjlCqpx2MFCKgqEofM
