1790270290387560	continuum-dev	itc:v3:AWKSTzM5JJnJPkQAAAAAQar23VW6voAAAAEykBY		item.comment	bn-2ri63	{"body":"cr-1s123d fixed in 04f5a4d8. (1) Every pinned-analysis vector is allocated at a precharged fixed capacity. The filtered axis now uses with_capacity(scratch.len()) plus extend. The PinnedTrace seam and a power-of-two boundary test (63..1025 members) cover capacity within charge, exact-limit replay, and a one-node-short refusal before allocation. The test kills the old collect. (2) The differential accepts a relaxed oracle refusal only for a pinned success. just check: fails only on the lead-owned security-review-present. dossier, lean, and test-policy pass separately."}	blake3:YtWuMvLl7cf4sG-cmC_MALRNxWZdZBhTqc-MzzcQ38o
1790270441534226	continuum-dev	itc:v3:AWKSTzM5JJnJPkQAAAAAQar23VW6voAAAAEykRY		item.comment	bn-2fk3	{"body":"cr-35ujnx fixed at 9a76dc7c. (1) The storage differential now keys the Submit count, so every quantity candidates() reads is in the pruning key. The count is re-pinned at 78,708 states and all 21 mutants are still caught. New neg-05 regression: Codex's two-path collision, plus a sweep over every config that finds no key with two candidate lists. The network and process generators read only config plus keyed sent/tickets lengths, so they have no mismatch. (2) The extern crate rule is now token-level over whole files, after a string-aware comment strip, in all five places: gov4_pack_kernel.py, INV-015 no_std_unconditional, and the three pack lanes. Only extern crate alloc; in lib.rs passes. Split and aliased std, core as c, alloc as a, and an extern hidden after a string containing // all fail. Each lane now also shows that a split, aliased extern crate std using s::fs compiles in dev and release but fails the structure rule. INV-015 and gov4 require that witness. New INV-015 test across the three packs, 2 new gov4 fixtures (both uncaught by the old checker), docs/12 §4 note updated. just check exit 1: governance stops at T09 'review gates' on the lead-owned independence-review finding. The skipped steps pass when run separately: revision delta, obligations self-test, dossier, lean, test-policy. .seal left untouched and uncommitted."}	blake3:5dWb87Eyegy9JmyTCOltwKix0-tAeXalpSraDA6yqjo
1790271297635796	continuum-dev	itc:v3:AWKSTzM5JJnJPkQAAAAAQar23VW6voAAAAEykhY		item.comment	bn-18w74	{"body":"cr-33e464 round 2 fixed at d0407fcd: protocol 3.9 / IDL 1.17. ErrorCode OutcomeUnknown (@since 3.9, not retryable) answers a custody write that passed its commit point unconfirmed. The authority is then quarantined (no signature, no signing write). A pending marker, written durably before the rename and cleared after a confirmed sync, carries the ambiguity across a crash. A relaunch loads the durable state, validates it, sweeps, and clears the marker. Pre-3.9 rule: with durable custody, signing.mint/rotate/revoke and intent.import_bundle are refused below 3.9 with UnsupportedSemanticFeature before anything changes; no custody means 3.8 unchanged. The crash oracle (KeystoreFaults::lose_rename) keeps the old or the new entry. every_answer_agrees_with_every_state_a_crash_can_leave covers mint, rotate, revoke and adopt: no success reloads the old state, and each OutcomeUnknown relaunch is one whole state, validated and signing. rule signing.custody (54->55 rules), RFC 0026 correction 58, RFC 0027 note, ADR-0054 amended. just check: fmt, lint, test, boundaries, covenant, dossier, lean and test-policy pass; only the lead-owned security-review-present (T09 review gates) fails. .seal left uncommitted."}	blake3:Yv7JTeiy8x_npzJlSiSmaEewA_9hYZBnFBqt21pFPy4
