1790271687360265	continuum-dev	itc:v3:AWKSTzM5JJnJPkQAAAAAQar23VW6voAAAAEylhY		item.comment	bn-35y4f	{"body":"Design-only stop, no commit. Re-deriving successors needs the model inside the kernel's input, and the CONTCERT v1 body carries only names, a domain, states and rows. So a wire change is required (proposed: wire epoch 2, carry the continuum-model/1 canonical encoding, merged with the bn-1m952 v2 design). No new dependency edge: RFC 0005 already puts the expression and transition-relation evaluators in kernel-core. Estimated +1,000 non-test lines in kernel-core. Design returned to the lead for a decision."}	blake3:r_qu1pcN2x6UgQ5Hal3oeLBD62iEElfZ7yBg6V2zl6s
1790271726343931	continuum-dev	itc:v3:AWKSTzM5JJnJPkQAAAAAQar23VW6voAAAAEylxY		item.comment	bn-35y4f	{"body":"Lead rulings on the design: certificate wire epoch 2 carries the model's canonical encoding, with state-index targets and an invariant property class, which merges bn-1m952. Rows are kept and must equal the re-derived relation. Epoch 1 stays decodable, but records certificate-model-correspondence as trusted. A C018 promotion, if the evidence supports it, is scoped to v2."}	blake3:XCLV51Q0KktN3T0S9N3afP2bjcTztg6qNDDTB6geeHY
1790271726378159	continuum-dev	itc:v3:AWKSTzM5JJnJPkQAAAAAQar23VW6voAAAAEymBY		item.comment	bn-1m952	{"body":"Merged into bn-35y4f by lead ruling: certificate wire v2 with state-index targets and an invariant property class, together with the model binding. Close this bone when bn-35y4f lands."}	blake3:QZV8AeEsD_DeVfU2bzVvTJ2xmCIbf9KRP9mdPlCV2oA
1790272078567627	continuum-dev	itc:v3:AWKSTzM5JJnJPkQAAAAAQar23VW6voAAAAEymRY		item.comment	bn-2fk3	{"body":"cr-35ujnx round 2 fixed at 7e93b446. One complete Rust token lexer (Reference, 2024) handles every literal kind: str, b, c, char, byte char with escapes incl. \\u{..}, and r, br, cr raw forms with any hash count. It also handles nested block comments, doc comments, lifetimes, labels and raw idents. Unlexable source fails closed as 'source the scan cannot lex': unterminated literals or comments, unbalanced raw hashes, unknown or reserved prefixes (x\"..\", #\"..\"), unknown escapes, string suffixes, and non-ASCII outside literals. It exists in two places. tools/governance/rust_lexer.py is used by gov4_pack_kernel.py. tools/governance/rust_lexer.rs is include!d by the INV-015 audit and the three lanes; there is no dependency edge. Both apply the same token-level structure rules. Corpus tools/governance/rust_lexer_cases.txt has 32 cases: an inside and a beside case per literal kind, one legit extern-in-string that must pass, and unlexable cases that must fail. INV-015 runs the corpus through all three packs. Each case is also a GOV-4-13 fixture (gov4-13-lexer-*), which runs the Python twin. A twin differential checks the two lexers token for token over the corpus and every pack source. The lane witness (split, aliased extern crate std compiles but fails the rule) is kept. docs/12 §4 updated. just check exit 1: governance stops at T09 'review gates' on the lead-owned independence-review finding only. The skipped steps pass separately. .seal untouched and uncommitted."}	blake3:l94KrpNNA1ZlPbxULt1z3JGs53flu-GlWyIFBD8rBXM
1790272384863377	continuum-dev	itc:v3:AWKSTzM5JJnJPkQAAAAAQar23VW6voAAAAEymhY		item.comment	bn-2lc0t	{"body":"Delivered at 853ac231 (test and prose only, no src logic change). Census: Carriage Field 26 / EnvelopeBudget 1 (new, isolation/resource-limits) / Handle 3 / StoredEvidence 5 / StoredContinuation 2 / Unlanded 11. New Reach census: Read 22 / CarriedUnread 4 (evidence.link: agent actors are refused before the body is read; a service-actor control shows the body is read) / RefusedAtAdmission 11 / Unlanded 11. Each Read outcome is pinned per case. evidence.link now names a held subject, and context.expand names a held pack in both suites. verification.start now names a real snapshot, and its budget comes from the payload. The reviser and steward now hold production_trace, so observe.ingest reaches the handler. Gate clauses: 2 held / 7 open, unchanged. FINDING: an all-absent Budget is accepted and runs at Bounds::CERTIFIABLE (budget.rs bounds_after). No RFC rule covers this, and plan 8.6 per-principal ceilings are not enforced. LOW-4: no wire path files a continuation (verification park mints the handle, startup restore checks derives_its_handle), so this is defence in depth only; TaskTable::park is public in-process API. Exit package 5.1 dated correction added. Adversarial opus pass: 4 MEDIUM + 5 LOW, fixed or documented. just check exit 0."}	blake3:269ooG-1Ca7m5it8odKP3UcWNZQQjtBDqPMDAcymptQ
1790272424238608	continuum-dev	itc:v3:AWKSTzM5JJnJPkQAAAAAQar23VW6voAAAAEymxY		item.comment	bn-2lc0t	{"body":"Review anchor: 01M3A8TJ3HS25V28F6WA0WPQ19 for cr-twfb12 (security review, head 853ac2319082)"}	blake3:u9YJEro1MQNkxKXCLFIY-lUrsY1SHalHWOEi7hWlG2A
1790272425094335	continuum-dev	itc:v3:AWKSTzM5JJnJPkQAAAAAQar23VW6voAAAAEynBY		item.create	bn-1wu3w	{"description":"Found by bn-2lc0t. RFC 0026 makes a budget REQUIRED, but a Budget with every dimension absent passes, and budget::bounds_after maps None to Bounds::CERTIFIABLE (2^20 states, 2^20 depth, 2^22 transitions). No RFC sentence defines an absent Budget dimension. Compare RFC 0027 B5, where output_policy absence is 'not no ceiling'. Plan §8.6 per-principal ceilings are not enforced, and only states is metered. Write the RFC rule for absent dimensions (a principal ceiling, not the maximum), enforce the per-principal ceilings, and meter every dimension. An RFC semantics change may affect clients; check whether it is a protocol change before implementing.","kind":"task","labels":["phase-b","req:phase-b","security","risk:high"],"title":"An all-absent verification Budget runs at CERTIFIABLE bounds; define absent-dimension semantics and a per-principal ceiling (bn-2lc0t finding)"}	blake3:R4L6TLMEbzX6KxCuPhWUXjb9uy_0RkbEGD34FYd_A74
