1790273334495829	continuum-dev	itc:v3:AWKSTzM5JJnJPkQAAAAAQar23VW6voAAAAEyoBY		item.comment	bn-20d8u	{"body":"Path (a) done in ws bn-20d8u, commit 2362760f. It needed no substrate change. SubstrateOp::Crash withdraws each live task's future unpolled. It ends the task record through complete_task(Panicked) and task_completed, and the leak audit is the fence. Journal encoding is v3: region-crashed, plus effect, obligation and time 'fenced'. region-settled gains a fenced set. The v2 grammar is still read, and v1 is no longer read. The lift and the independent A7 model have crash rules: stopped set, fences first in canonical order, no late timer, no subtree under cancellation, and Unsupported for cancel, deadline or channel holders. The register runs with CrashMode::FailStop. Its projection reads Lose from the crash, and Quiescence and Conservation count fences apart. The fail-stop baseline has 0 findings. M02 is detected on the same 24 runs. M03 is excluded by TaskCrashed. M07 is detected. M08 is excluded, with 3875 timers fenced and 0 fired after the crash. continuum-asupersync is BOUNDARY, not semantic core, so there is no GOV record. RFC 0026 correction 58 is added. The protocol and IDL are unchanged. The opus pre-review found 1 blocker and 4 should-fix items. All are fixed, except that an unsupported crash ends judgement, which is documented in c58. just check exit 0."}	blake3:7Vwpt3NlYv-ICDM-Ogwsawf3ZJKm39FjkcvZUITa974
1790273376703802	continuum-dev	itc:v3:AWKSTzM5JJnJPkQAAAAAQar23VW6voAAAAEyoRY		item.comment	bn-20d8u	{"body":"Review anchor: 01M3A9QMB3B68M57001TT93MT2 for cr-1a6akb (security review, head ffdf3a319847)"}	blake3:lWa845uDTxhirKiAswYp0V_xNqDYR3D_vN3YbQMoWQc
1790273593138336	continuum-dev	itc:v3:AWKSTzM5JJnJPkQAAAAAQar23VW6voAAAAEyohY		item.comment	bn-18w74	{"body":"cr-33e464 round 4 fixed at c6715143. validate_custody now checks every audit record against its link or entry, and every link or entry against its record. Own rotation/compromise revocation -> own link. Peer rotation -> adopted link (Codex case -> AdoptedLink). Peer compromise revocation -> exactly one of adopted link or local entry. Peer loss revocation -> local entry. Supersession -> both keys own. A mint needs nothing. Reverse: links must be recorded, and local entries must name revoked peer keys. New persisted state field local_revocations (a local revoke of a peer carries no link). Test every_record_keeps_its_link_or_entry_across_a_restart removes each piece and adds each unaccounted entry. just check run recipe by recipe in the foreground: fmt, lint, every package's tests, boundaries, covenant, dossier, lean, test-policy pass. Only the lead-owned security-review-present (T09 review gates) fails. .seal left out."}	blake3:KU6PcvOeI3hdDlfpsd9weX7v2bRg_0_iz2SupDF3ZAw
