1790273808658924	continuum-dev	itc:v3:AWKSTzM5JJnJPkQAAAAAQar23VW6voAAAAEyphY		item.comment	bn-2fk3	{"body":"cr-35ujnx round 3 (th-3e2339) fixed at 8df11ca7. Storage: the reference model is now Model{mutant, config, state: State, events}. The transition is a method of State and reads only state, config, mutant and step. The pruning key is the whole State: nodes, logs, stable, tickets, crashes, submitted, steps, retained. StorageConfig gains with_max_steps (1..=MAX_STEPS, ConfigRefusal::StepsOutOfRange) and the journal header carries it. Every differential config has a small step bound that binds (8, and 3 in one). New mutant StepBoundOffByOne. 66,753 states, 22 mutants caught. neg-05 now checks, over every config, that two histories with one key have the same outcome, event and successor key for every candidate. New neg-06 pins the Lab's fields to the compared view (events.len() added). Network and process audit: their keys omitted the journal length and, except under the budget config, the retained bytes, while the Lab reads both. Fixed: both are now keyed, the models apply the MAX_STEPS refusal, every config has a binding budget, and a collision test was added to each. Network 24,371 states and process 21,819, all mutants still caught. Their MAX_STEPS stays 1<<20 and is unreachable in exploration: a configurable bound there is a pack src change and needs a GOV-4 record, so I left it for the lead. START_HERE annotations updated. just check exit 1: governance stops at T09 'review gates' on the lead-owned independence-review finding only. The skipped steps pass separately. .seal untouched and uncommitted."}	blake3:F8KAaIlT0XavwZ0awxTNl7-hVameH1PHfuoFxrh_2sM
