1790275297302578	continuum-dev	itc:v3:AWKSTzM5JJnJPkQAAAAAQar23VW6voAAAAEysBY		item.comment	bn-2fk3	{"body":"cr-35ujnx round 4 fixed at 927601b0. Class-level rule: both lexer twins (tools/governance/rust_lexer.py and .rs) now hold an AMBIENT set of every compile-time input a pack can read from its build environment: env, option_env, include, include_str, include_bytes, file, cfg, cfg_attr. It is refused as a token anywhere, so a path (::core::option_env) or a space before ! changes nothing. Inside literals and comments it does not count. build.rs and links stay refused by the manifest rule; proc macros need a dependency, which is also refused. Compiler evidence: each of the three lanes reads rustc's dep-info for the dev and release builds of the real pack and requires no '# env-dep:' line and no file outside src/. A copy that reads option_env!(CONTINUUM_LANE_MODE) compiles, its dep-info names the variable (so the empty set is meaningful), and the structure rule refuses it. INV-015 and gov4 LANE_MARKERS require this witness. New: 10 corpus cases and 10 gov4 fixtures (8 violations, one per macro plus cfg and a spaced path; 2 clean, in a literal and in a comment); INV-015 per-macro leg mutants for all three packs; a Rust/Python rules-parity test (--rules). Pack lib docs and docs/12 §4 updated. just check exit 1: governance stops at T09 'review gates' on the lead-owned independence-review finding only. The skipped steps pass separately. .seal untouched and uncommitted."}	blake3:ABS0sFB26gA26HWAx0eWvqm_uQYJj0t2WNDSl6lyyug
1790276161151491	continuum-dev	itc:v3:AWKSTzM5JJnJPkQAAAAAQar23VW6voAAAAEysRY		item.comment	bn-35y4f	{"body":"Implemented at 5cef33c9 in ws bn-35y4f (bn-1m952 merged per lead ruling). CONTCERT wire epoch 2: the certificate carries the continuum-model/1 encoding; kernel-core decodes it with its own decoder (src/model.rs), precharges work, checks Dom(M), Init(M), exact row equality (u32 indices, range-checked) and an invariant class. Epoch 1 decodable; its claims keep certificate-model-correspondence. C018 lane rerun: producer 8 caught / 2 missed (identity.rs encoder) / 3 refused, was 4/7/1; checker 33/35 killed. Claim-A register cert 14,697,631 bytes (was 117 MB), about 0.22 s release, all 3 invariants verified. C018 -> OBSERVED scoped to epoch-2 finite closure, baseline revision bn-35y4f. Kernel +1699 lines (total 12684). just check exit 1: governance stops at T09 review gates (lead-owned kernel-reviewers and security-review); remaining recipes run separately and pass."}	blake3:ymVpopEZMVPk9vcs9Pv3BbcsdYgagodq39k5vc6ZBCk
1790276270669686	continuum-dev	itc:v3:AWKSTzM5JJnJPkQAAAAAQar23VW6voAAAAEyshY		item.comment	bn-35y4f	{"body":"Review anchor: 01M3ACFYF3N9YFYM48B2HB83GC for cr-18l29w (security review, head b46ad70dfac6)"}	blake3:pV1fzx0EjSAMhDl9o29Ks-m6sp5s-ReUh-s_G6GI2pQ
1790276280781448	continuum-dev	itc:v3:AWKSTzM5JJnJPkQAAAAAQar23VW6voAAAAEysxY		item.create	bn-3hk4v	{"description":"bn-35y4f: the kernel re-derives the finite-closure relation from the model a certificate carries, but continuumd marks every verified certificate alike (epoch 1 or 2) and never compares the claim's carried model encoding with the model the daemon holds for that snapshot. Until it does, model binding is library-only on the system path. Require epoch 2 (or refuse/downgrade claims whose trusted components include certificate-model-correspondence) and compare encodings, fail closed on mismatch or absence; typed outcome per INV-008.","kind":"task","labels":["phase-b","req:phase-b","req:c018","security"],"title":"C018 system path: continuumd requires certificate epoch 2 and compares the carried model encoding with the model it holds (bn-35y4f follow-up)"}	blake3:fkKqbdXD_BZbkTLMQUtP1bt23lAbGSBFkIvtZ-lLdcY
1790276280997414	continuum-dev	itc:v3:AWKSTzM5JJnJPkQAAAAAQar23VW6voAAAAEytBY		item.create	bn-cyxt4	{"description":"bn-35y4f mutant rerun: 2 misses are encoder faults (dropped initial state, widened domain) in identity.rs. An encoder that drops content defines a different model and the certificate is true of that model, so identity.rs (395 lines) remains in the trusted component list. Options: an independent re-encoding from CML source in the checking path, a differential against a second encoder, or a stated trust with a size cap.","kind":"task","labels":["phase-b","req:phase-b","req:c018"],"title":"C018: the model encoder (continuum-model-core identity.rs) stays trusted; decide how to remove or bound it (bn-35y4f follow-up)"}	blake3:teo4BbHJJIkzSQzofs9MYhDmeDh2YiBA5D5s842Aho0
