1790277024803728	continuum-dev	itc:v3:AWKSTzM5JJnJPkQAAAAAQar23VW6voAAAAEyvhY		item.comment	bn-18w74	{"body":"cr-1dc5ii (MEDIUM, CWE-362) fixed at 0a811cfa. LocalKeystore is no longer Clone (compile_fail doctest). Every write runs under the handle's writer mutex, which owns the lifetime-locked descriptor or takes the flock for that write alone. A read-only open from another handle takes a shared flock and is refused (Locked) while a holder lives, in process or out. Each write uses its own signing-state.tmp-<serial>, created O_EXCL, and the sweep clears leftovers. Tests: concurrent_writes_through_one_handle_are_serialized, a_second_handle_in_process_is_refused_while_one_holds_the_store. The crash-oracle and custody suites pass. just check run recipe by recipe in the foreground: all pass except the lead-owned security-review-present (T09 review gates). .seal left out."}	blake3:OP8ewjtwJtDAyAyOlZRyV4iYvX4wDXxI-JdEF8LYrVg
1790277072949761	continuum-dev	itc:v3:AWKSTzM5JJnJPkQAAAAAQar23VW6voAAAAEyvxY		item.comment	bn-2fk3	{"body":"cr-35ujnx round 5 (th-dbwhy1) fixed at 29796151. Manifest text scans are gone from the lanes and INV-015. The shared include tools/governance/rust_lexer.rs gains mod cargo_view: a small JSON parser, cargo metadata (--format-version 1 --no-deps --offline, plus --locked in the real workspace), and pack_problem. pack_problem requires no custom-build or proc-macro target, links null, no dependency, no feature, and one lib at the pack's src/lib.rs. A Cargo error is a refusal. Lanes: the real pack is checked in its real workspace (--locked) and the control copy after cargo check; the lane asserts no env-dep:OUT_DIR. Nine manifest variants are refused per lane for all three packs: quoted build key, single-quoted links key with build.rs, dotted package.\"links\", build.workspace, inline-table package with build, keyless build.rs, std feature, target dependency, dependency table. INV-015: manifest_problem evaluates any manifest in a scratch copy of the real workspace (root Cargo.toml verbatim) with Cargo; [lints] is checked structurally with tomllib. The boundary legs use cargo metadata --locked in place of declared_dependencies/contains(\"build\"). New INV-015 test refuses the same forms for all three packs and accepts a quoted \"workspace\" = true. gov4 (tomllib, structural) gets 5 new fixtures; the dotted one is a TOML error and fails closed. gov4 LANE_MARKERS and the INV-015 lane check require the cargo-view check. Docs updated. just check exit 1: governance stops at T09 'review gates' on the lead-owned independence-review finding only. The skipped steps pass separately. .seal untouched and uncommitted."}	blake3:PnDY1cZBGu38VTeK6YisfAR3fQVLvR42CveaSKfYvvU
1790277323668438	continuum-dev	itc:v3:AWKSTzM5JJnJPkQAAAAAQar23VW6voAAAAEywBY		item.comment	bn-162z4	{"body":"Delivered at ea06585f (test-only, both files under crates/continuumd/tests/). g2_injection_corpus_evidence.rs: added protocol_floor(operation)/case_protocol_version(operation), a second independent reader over notes/plan/schemas/continuumd-native-protocol.idl's own @since text (mechanical, not registry::introduced_at). envelope() now negotiates max(op floor, corpus baseline) per operation instead of a fixed version. SIGNING_WIRE_PROBES + probe()/run_probe() deleted; the six protocol-3.8 operations (signing.mint/rotate/revoke/sign_pack, intent.export_bundle/import_bundle) are now SIGNING_WIRE_CASES, six ordinary Case values run through the same envelope/frame/plant/carriage/run machinery as every corpus case, each on its own fixture_at(case_protocol_version(op)) connection (a case names no protocol version and RFC 0026 negotiates one version per connection, baked into Daemon at construction — no mid-run reconnect exists). carriage()/plant() gained a Carriage::PrivilegeProbe variant for the four field-less bodies. Kept local to this file, not added to continuum-security's ratified 48-case CASES corpus (growing that taxonomy is a research/35 decision), so the CASES-scoped Carriage census (26/1/3/5/2/11, unchanged), Reach census (22/4/11/11, unchanged), and gate_g2_07_acceptance.rs's admission-matrix/gate-clauses tests are all untouched. version() (corpus baseline) moves 3.2 -> 3.3 = CASES.iter().map(protocol_floor).max(), driven by evidence.link's own @since(\"3.3\"): the only way every existing case also satisfies its own new negotiated>=floor obligation without a second connection; nothing in this daemon behaves differently between 3.2 and 3.3 (next real gate is 3.7's CapabilityDescriptor.instances, then 3.8's signing wire), and a new pinned test asserts that boundary so crossing it later is a decision. negotiated_at()'s implemented-version list now derives from registry::PROTOCOL_VERSION instead of a hardcoded [3.1,3.2,3.8], so protocol 3.9 (bn-18w74) is negotiable and its operations' floors picked up with no code change here. Tests: 34 -> 39 (added: no-case-below-its-floor, no-@since-gives-the-sentinel, unknown-op-panics, and a cross-check that this file's independent floor agrees with registry::introduced_at wherever the daemon truly gates one). gate_g2_07_acceptance.rs: cosmetic sync only (SIGNING_WIRE_PROBES -> SIGNING_WIRE_CASES in prose and its source-text scan, test count 34 -> 39); its own CASES-scoped counts and admission matrix untouched. Perf: the IDL-reading functions (idl_source/idl_privileged_operations/idl_since_versions/idl_operation_names) are now memoized per-process via OnceLock — envelope() calls them on the order of hundreds of times per run and the uncached version took ~35-70s for this one file vs ~0.4s cached; still read from disk, just once. Adversarial opus subagent pass: no HIGH/MEDIUM findings; 3 LOW (checked and disposed): (1) since_above could silently miss an unusual @since spelling and fall back to NO_FLOOR — fixed by adding the_mechanically_derived_floor_agrees_with_every_operation_the_daemon_actually_gates, a cross-check against registry::introduced_at over all 83 operations; (2) the baseline could later drift into behaviourally different territory (3.7+) with no signal if a future ratified case used a higher-@since op — fixed by adding the_corpus_baseline_has_not_drifted_into_a_behaviourally_different_version, pinning version() < 3.7; (3) no_case_negotiates_a_protocol_version_below_its_operations_since checks >= rather than exact equality with the fixture's negotiated version — accepted as-is, since a mismatch already fails loudly at dispatch (RFC 0026 step 1) and every case here is built through fixture_at(case_protocol_version(op)), which sets both to the same value by construction. just check: exit 0 (fmt, clippy --workspace --all-targets -D warnings, full workspace test, boundaries, covenant, governance, dossier, lean, test-policy)."}	blake3:gppVgg9clSjEDapp1-0DI-5uO4sQpHob7-GlGCfExIg
1790277366156912	continuum-dev	itc:v3:AWKSTzM5JJnJPkQAAAAAQar23VW6voAAAAEywRY		item.create	bn-7xz8v	{"description":"bn-162z4: the daemon's hand-kept registry::introduced_at gate table covers 8 operations. evidence.link carries @since(3.3) in the IDL but is served on a 3.2 connection. rule versioning (RFC 0026) requires refusing an operation the negotiated version does not define. Derive the gate from the IDL @since of every operation (generated or checked table, with a test that every IDL op with @since above the window floor is gated), and refuse with the typed code the RFC names. Check whether any other op is similarly ungated.","kind":"task","labels":["phase-b","req:phase-b","security"],"title":"continuumd serves operations below their IDL @since: registry::introduced_at gates only 8 of 83 operations (bn-162z4 finding)"}	blake3:gMthYT90IR0sR958WQLIvGA4YHxQvnZeo2al4xXd6aU
