1790280340448503	continuum-dev	itc:v3:AWKSTzM5JJnJPkQAAAAAQar23VW6voAAAAEy3RY		item.comment	bn-18w74	{"body":"cr-1dc5ii round 2 fixed at 21d4166c. (1) While custody is unconfirmed: verify is standing-stale; a bundle accept is AcceptanceChainInvalid; import (incl. a zero-fact retry), local accept, lock and registry are refused typed with nothing changed. (2) The lifetime lock records its owning pid (/proc/self); a fork copy is refused (InheritedHandle); descriptors are CLOEXEC; a real spawned child inherits nothing and gets Locked. Custody launch is Linux/Android only, a documented residual. (3) A replayed answer is held to the negotiated version after the authority check; a 3.9 OutcomeUnknown is never replayed to 3.8; an emission backstop covers fresh answers. (4) TEST-9-07 binds behavioral regressions for every path. The fresh-opus pass found no blockers; S1-S6 fixed (local accept/lock gate, replay check order, Linux residual documented, end-to-end acceptance test, non-vacuous spawn test, accessor docs). just check run recipe by recipe in the foreground: only the lead-owned security-review-present (T09 review gates) fails."}	blake3:_XQIqe_hEmGi6htkc5zry2G61rqfx3a0EbJ6pkPjTJE
1790280530735776	continuum-dev	itc:v3:AWKSTzM5JJnJPkQAAAAAQar23VW6voAAAAEy3hY		item.comment	bn-3hk4v	{"body":"d2ba3c69 in ws bn-3hk4v. evidence.verify is the only daemon path that accepts a certificate as evidence. A verified claim now reaches validated only when two things hold. (1) It trusts nothing beyond envelope-digest-binding. (2) Its carried continuum-model/1 encoding equals, byte for byte, Model::identity() of the model the daemon holds for the one sealed snapshot the node names in provenance.inputs. The snapshot is resolved as verification.start resolves it. A mismatch is CertificateRejected with no data. Epoch 1, state type, temporal, LRAT and SMT claims, and a missing, ambiguous, unsealed or unregistered snapshot, are InsufficientEvidence. Inputs are checked against the grant before the kernel runs. No IDL change and no new code. Tests: new c018_model_binding_system_path.rs (11 tests, 6 fail on the old daemon). daemon_evidence, pr7 and g2 fixtures now name a sealed Die Hard snapshot. The temporal Verified pin was flipped to InsufficientEvidence. docs/18 C018 scope and residuals are updated, plus an RFC 0005 note and a claims-baseline revision. just check exit 0. Adversarial opus pass: 9 findings. Fixed SAT/SMT, pre-kernel scope, and ws-class content confusion. Documented property binding, catalog trust and replay as residuals."}	blake3:u-fIa4Aye20IlJTWC2EvrqBDzKCzlMWbCAalqattDpE
1790280564786857	continuum-dev	itc:v3:AWKSTzM5JJnJPkQAAAAAQar23VW6voAAAAEy3xY		item.comment	bn-3hk4v	{"body":"Review anchor: 01M3AGJZYZZE4M0JF09XPA966S for cr-3lrkq3 (security review, head b33db584bcab)"}	blake3:t2PQNJoZKiMCmFMqd4KIgmDZ2FGseKvs88MIUvN7LuI
1790280592397106	continuum-dev	itc:v3:AWKSTzM5JJnJPkQAAAAAQar23VW6voAAAAEy4BY		item.create	bn-9032b	{"description":"bn-3hk4v binds the carried model to the snapshot's model, but (1) the claim's property (invariant token, property and scope digests) is not compared with the evidence node's claim or its intent, so a true certificate of a different property of the same model validates; (2) an idempotent replay under a narrower capability of the same actor returns the earlier answer without re-checking the snapshot grant. Fix both, fail closed, typed.","kind":"task","labels":["phase-b","req:phase-b","req:c018","security","risk:high"],"title":"evidence.verify: bind the certificate claim's property to the node's claim or intent, and re-check the snapshot on idempotent replay under a narrower capability (bn-3hk4v residuals)"}	blake3:RR22kFmAFmfcDG0LepiCD42UdLuGQq4zIB5zlNWZ2yY
