1790281707978497	continuum-dev	itc:v3:AWKSTzM5JJnJPkQAAAAAQar23VW6voAAAAEy7hY		item.comment	bn-fxxf2	{"body":"Added WorkerStep::Crash to the calculus (continuum-task). It moves Created, Running or Suspended to Failed in any cancel phase, discards staged slots, and leaves substrate obligations owed with a terminal holder. lift_crash now takes Crash, with no injected Resume. RFC 0026 correction 59 is added and correction 58 item 3 is amended. The continuumd oracle gains Crash and CrashB: pin 8,020/58,455 moves to 10,575/86,331, and 5 new mutants are told apart. The fail_stop_crash calculus replay differential is pinned: all 1,952 corpus journals replay and match the lift state, and Fail-only refuses all 1,952. On 13,373 mutants the two agree at the same event and fault, and 64 crash-program journals cover a running crash. The journal, the A7 model and the goldens are unchanged. The GOV record is tools/governance/reviews/bn-fxxf2.toml. The opus pre-review found 0 blockers, 3 should-fix and 5 nits, all fixed. just check: fmt, lint, test, boundaries and covenant pass. dossier, lean and test-policy pass when run apart. governance fails only on the lead-owned security-review-present item."}	blake3:jsaxHMvKbuc3AH7Joj_ZQTFhQUpsqm3SkwTSqVDDxaU
