1790282597169857	continuum-dev	itc:v3:AWKSTzM5JJnJPkQAAAAAQar23VW6voAAAAEy-BY		item.comment	bn-18w74	{"body":"cr-1dc5ii round 3 (CWE-667) fixed at fe0364c8. The owner pid moved out of the writer mutex into an AtomicU32 written once. owned_here() runs before any lock on load_or_mint, guard (persist, mint), open_shared and sweep. Drop only closes the child's descriptor (no unlock), so the parent's flock survives. No other mutex is on the custody path. Test an_inherited_handle_is_refused_even_while_its_mutex_is_held parks a write that holds the mutex, then requires InheritedHandle within 10s for write, read and sweep. The lock-first mutant times out. It sits in tests/ with a hidden simulate_fork_copy seam, because INV-015 bars std::thread/std::time in keystore.rs. just check run recipe by recipe in the foreground: only the lead-owned security-review-present (T09 review gates) fails. One unreproduced keystore-test failure appeared once (open at tests/keystore.rs:378); 21 reruns and the gate run were clean."}	blake3:kaAuQAeFglZQh3I_Gx9jHsqp-vA-nwM7NTfUL9NlM8E
