1790284590915080	continuum-dev	itc:v3:AWKSTzM5JJnJPkQAAAAAQar23VW6voAAAAEyhhc		item.comment	bn-24a5c	{"body":"f4e20400: engine-reference reads X#defined on every checking path. Invariant, deadlock and liveness outcomes gain a typed Undefined (precedence: eval error, undefined action read, undefined invariant read, violation, holds/inconclusive; RFC 0003 names no order, so it follows bn-31vf). Witness targets on a predicate end only where its reads are defined. Both closure emitters refuse an undefined read (EmissionError::Undefined). model-core owns DEFINED_SUFFIX/definedness_subject and a fail-closed Definedness classifier (cml-elab re-exports it). continuumd refuses an unrefuted campaign with an undefined read as UnsupportedSemanticFeature. Tests: definedness_differential.rs (2000-case corpus vs an independent Option evaluator, kernel verdicts on emitted certs, bounded runs, metamorphic reorder/alpha-rename), register.rs pin flipped from Violated to Undefined, inv008 daemon refusal test. C018 evidence regenerated. just check: fmt/lint/test/boundaries/covenant pass; governance fails only on GOV-4-06 security-review-present (lead-owned); dossier, lean, test-policy pass when run separately. Kernel gap: continuum-kernel-core check.rs invariant closure ignores definedness (needs a separate bone). bn-31vf tests/differential.rs needs an Undefined arm after this merges."}	blake3:xPOW11b7RvULvc9s-w72mAV7Ly6jxnvq6GM8V-5BT-U
1790284633884180	continuum-dev	itc:v3:AWKSTzM5JJnJPkQAAAAAQar23VW6voAAAAEyhxc		item.create	bn-iu8eh	{"description":"bn-24a5c: crates/continuum-kernel-core/src/check.rs (about lines 173-190 and 272-288) checks invariant and state-domain closures without reading I#defined or A#defined. RFC 0003 Definedness: a state violating X#defined is the typed outcome undefined read in X, and RFC 0013 says an undefined result invalidates the model. A certificate from a producer other than engine-reference (which now refuses such emissions) over an undefined read would verify. The kernel's own decoder/evaluator (src/model.rs, bn-35y4f) must classify definedness predicates independently of model-core (continuum-model-core definedness.rs from bn-24a5c is the producer-side reference; the kernel may not depend on it) and reject/typed-unsupported a closure with an undefined read. Kernel change: GOV 4 two reviewers, C018 evidence rerun.","kind":"task","labels":["phase-b","req:phase-b","req:c018","security","risk:high"],"title":"Kernel finite-closure check ignores definedness: a certificate over an undefined read verifies (bn-24a5c finding)"}	blake3:Q3qX3FwJZsOzHOThsjem-mEHKiOAIMkuu2x--kheQOs
