1790284704912733	continuum-dev	itc:v3:AWKSTzM5JJnJPkQAAAAAQar23VW6voAAAAEyjhc		item.comment	bn-18w74	{"body":"Round-4 fork window closed at 173c6514. The owner pid is recorded in LocalKeystore::new, before any lock. owned_here() runs before every lock (first load, first-use mint, persist, sweep, open). An unreadable pid is refused (Unsupported), never treated as free. Drop takes no lock. The ordering table is in the type doc. The fork-window test parks a mutex-holding write in the first-use mint, a held write and a transient write; the fork copy must answer InheritedHandle within 10s at each; plus a first-load test. The flake had a real cause: the two process-spawning tests fork before exec, and the child briefly holds a copy of a concurrent test's flock, which then reads Locked. They moved to tests/keystore_processes.rs, serialized. Before: 4 of 25 parallel runs failed. After: 50 + 10 runs at load 29 were clean. The window is documented as a typed, fail-closed residual. just check run recipe by recipe in the foreground: only the lead-owned security-review-present (T09 review gates) fails."}	blake3:04q1udQ4sgDZtbtsckm1Jqe2l6WP9bO5-q9K-5D9JmY
