1790284953289118	continuum-dev	itc:v3:AWKSTzM5JJnJPkQAAAAAQar23VW6voAAAAEykBc		item.comment	bn-1oj6	{"body":"cr-37bshu: MEDIUM fixed in b9ddf1c1 and bc8bae22. Service discovery now rests on a new fixed-addressing assumption, with a stale-resolution test; the network profile is re-pinned at 0.2.0. HIGH not fixed, stopped as instructed: intent-contract.schema.json fault_model.profiles is a bare string array (RFC 0037: profile names), with no field to pin a profile version or fingerprint. RFC 0037 W8 and RFC 0027 put the pack pin in the snapshot's domain_packs digests, so the fix needs a schema or RFC decision from the lead. just check: only the missing [pack.independence_review] fails (check_obligations and T09 review gates). dossier, lean and test-policy pass."}	blake3:F-Fw8sZzPkYTdyjDTuoc2oDZlLfGxvXI5LQEfSs407A
1790285243087122	continuum-dev	itc:v3:AWKSTzM5JJnJPkQAAAAAQar23VW6voAAAAEykRc		item.comment	bn-ympz5	{"body":"Fixed both kernel-review findings (cr-18l29w). (1) receipt.rs: Receipt::wire_epoch_id() is now per-instance, set from CheckedClaim::wire_epoch() -- an epoch-1 cert's receipt names CONTCERT/1, epoch-2 names CONTCERT/2. checker.version keeps naming the checker's newest-supported epoch (2), documented as deliberate. No wire/schema change; to_json() output unchanged, so no golden re-bless. (2) model.rs/check.rs: evaluator depth-budget exhaustion is now Fault::DepthExhausted, routed via a new WalkFault enum and testable walk_fault() fn to Unsupported(ResourceBound{ExpressionDepth}), never Rejected(EvaluationOverflow). Unreachable via any decoder-accepted certificate today (decoder depth_bound == evaluator's starting budget); this guards against a future divergence false-rejecting. Invariant-loop Fault match made exhaustive by name. Tests added: receipt epoch1-vs-epoch2 test, direct evaluator depth-exhaustion unit tests (model.rs, check.rs), a walk_fault routing unit test, a metamorphic wire_epoch() invariance check, and differential/corpus regression guards. Adversarial opus review ran; addressed all 4 non-blocking findings (added the walk_fault unit test, made the invariant match exhaustive, removed a debug_assert! I'd added that violates KCOV-05 no-panic-escape and rewrote that doc honestly, fixed the governance record's mutation_tests list). tools/tcb-audit evidence regenerated (mutants.toml anchor tracked the refactor); tools/governance/reviews/bn-ympz5.toml added ([kernel.reviewers]/[semantic.security_review] left for lead); its self-test fixtures' hardcoded kernel line-count totals bumped. just check: passes except the one expected governance failure (missing [kernel.reviewers]/[semantic.security_review], lead-owned) -- fmt/lint/test/boundaries/covenant/dossier/lean/test-policy all verified passing independently. Commit afabea76."}	blake3:dufcpQI1KkOnnK9MXAhqDq_LWGmDaE1wNyNmDG7SF7s
