1790285658135590	continuum-dev	itc:v3:AWKSTzM5JJnJPkQAAAAAQar23VW6voAAAAEylhc		item.comment	bn-9032b	{"body":"Part (1) stopped, no code change. The evidence node records no property identity to compare with the certificate claim. evidence-graph-node.schema.json has kind, artifact, claim_id, labels, provenance.inputs and no property, invariant, scope or intent member. IDL rule evidence.claim_identity says claim_id is an opaque grouping key and forbids resolving a property identifier to it. Envelope property_digest and scope_digest have no preimage defined in any RFC or schema. No wire op appends a certificate node and verification.start emits no certificate, so no Target is tied to one. Snapshot -> IntentHandle reaches the intent's claims, but the node names no claim, and no RFC maps an intent claim (CPNF AST) to a model invariant token. Binding needs a design decision: a node member or a provenance.inputs convention naming the property, plus a defined property_digest/scope_digest preimage. Lead decision required."}	blake3:iLfE14RIa1l1VXgTTraQRS82QyYFOxB3icftZLiUNOc
1790285680585126	continuum-dev	itc:v3:AWKSTzM5JJnJPkQAAAAAQar23VW6voAAAAEylxc		item.link	bn-9032b	{"link_type":"blocks","target":"bn-1gych"}	blake3:kmQLg7AOHZjr84IrYetKK4kDiYreNJVjbA-7b-qbLBU
1790285680624309	continuum-dev	itc:v3:AWKSTzM5JJnJPkQAAAAAQar23VW6voAAAAEymBc		item.comment	bn-9032b	{"body":"Lead: blocked on a privileged design decision. The evidence-node schema has no property carrier, and property_digest/scope_digest have no normative preimage (worker finding above). Needs, together with bn-1gych: where a certificate node names its property (schema member or RFC 0005/0038 inputs rule), the digest preimages, and a write path. Protocol/schema change in Phase B, so it goes to the user."}	blake3:wgsoQrjMST0WtYyRmwV5vqyA0uDqwupuBQfp-38hogA
