1790285784691443	continuum-dev	itc:v3:AWKSTzM5JJnJPkQAAAAAQar23VW6voAAAAEynBc		item.comment	bn-1eld5	{"body":"Scope note (bn-1oj6, cr-37bshu, lead ruling c1): pinning is now by name. A pack profile name identifies its canonical bytes (RFC 0002 correction 1, docs/12 §4). Each pack keeps every published profile byte for byte (-v0 frozen at 0.1.0, -v1 at 1.0.0), and a per-pack registry test (pr15-impl04-hon-03) pins every (name, fingerprint) pair, so a content change under a published name fails the build. A contract moves to -v1 only through an intent revision; the library-path evidence is crates/continuum-semantic-diff/tests/pr15_impl04_profile_revision.rs. Remaining, not required now: a structured pin in the contract (version and digest per profile under a schema_epoch advance). Also open: RFC 0031 classifies an added profile by membership only, so a profile whose declared assumptions are a superset is an ordinary added fault record (verdict allow under no-removal), not an assumption strengthening."}	blake3:wnnh_WbJrLxcv6QHmN6i1k9ATnpg_d9_xjsEBGxIRr4
1790285836384999	continuum-dev	itc:v3:AWKSTzM5JJnJPkQAAAAAQar23VW6voAAAAEynRc		item.comment	bn-31vf	{"body":"cr-174gtd round 2 (780500ed, c06bc26c): audit derives its own basis (source, limits, epoch label, function versions pinned to REGISTRY, fail closed); CleanRun and Revision basis fields private; parity and cone share one completeness check, cone checks the earlier run's source; normalized identity precharged by a stated bound (256/node, covers escaped strings, checked on corpus + adversarial model); wire() removed and explain claim narrowed (ADR residual); trace revises each edit once (counted_revisions 17 lanes / 18 traces, quarantine_reruns asserted). Golden: lane totals unchanged; traces moved (promotion reuses Exact 44->53, Conservative 11->13; explored 114->82) because the double-run is gone. Adversarial pass done, fixed. just check: only governance security-review-present (lead-owned); dossier/lean/test-policy pass."}	blake3:U1yAXsVuBD52rhTYkd0-PRo8rUO_KI1Eb93TAzbFiVU
1790286611299509	continuum-dev	itc:v3:AWKSTzM5JJnJPkQAAAAAQar23VW6voAAAAEynhc		item.comment	bn-ympz5	{"body":"Kernel review nit (th-29pkc4): receipt.rs certificate_wire_epoch_id fallback would label a future epoch 3 as CONTCERT/2; when adding an epoch, replace it with a match on named constants or an enum."}	blake3:OgUc2u-1rcoJ0U-_xBB7PSCExPzQK_vRS-0JQfME8so
