1790286745241818	continuum-dev	itc:v3:AWKSTzM5JJnJPkQAAAAAQar23VW6voAAAAEyoBc		item.comment	bn-24a5c	{"body":"5aec4627 (cr-pt5h3a): definedness follows every chain whole. model-core Definedness classifies each #defined predicate by its chain base, deepest first; a chain with a gap or through an action name is read as an action's (fail closed). The scan, witnesses (guards_of), liveness and both emitters read every member. New tests/definedness_nested.rs (7 tests; the 4 original ones fail on an export of 0a5c152a). The corpus (4000 cases) and oracle now generate nested, gap and orphan chains; nested_decisive=580. model-core unit tests cover chains. C018 evidence regenerated. just check: governance stops only on GOV-4-06 security-review-present (lead-owned); fmt/lint/test/boundaries/covenant pass; dossier, lean, test-policy pass when run separately."}	blake3:sYVMRdADf6Okpzt821cpTAmBirusmcCWsxEI4WtNtNs
1790286793358763	continuum-dev	itc:v3:AWKSTzM5JJnJPkQAAAAAQar23VW6voAAAAEyoRc		item.create	bn-1eoco	{"description":"bn-24a5c (cr-pt5h3a) found the definedness classifier looked only at a single #defined suffix; nested chains, gaps, and chains through action names escaped. model-core Definedness::of now classifies whole chains and fails closed. bn-31vf's incremental engine and its independent audit scan only depth-1 guards, and its tests/differential.rs matches CheckOutcome exhaustively. After both merge: use the chain rule (engine via model-core; audit independently), map CheckOutcome::Undefined to the typed Undefined in the differential as a real comparison, update lib.rs's oracle note.","kind":"task","labels":["phase-b","req:phase-b","req:pr-22a"],"title":"continuum-incremental: definedness scan uses the model-core chain rule (nested #defined, fail-closed), and the differential compares CheckOutcome::Undefined (bn-24a5c follow-up)"}	blake3:AjHB8ooR0slmuPNhBPu3oB-nHfeZUCTxgpzhjH7WWV8
