1790288642473048	continuum-dev	itc:v3:AWKSTzM5JJnJPkQAAAAAQar23VW6voAAAAEytRc		item.comment	bn-24a5c	{"body":"980f6673 (cr-pt5h3a round 2): the chain walk now starts at the member's full name. A chain guards a predicate only if no name of it (base, intermediate, full member name) is an action name or schema, or contains '(' (reads as an instance); any collision fails closed as an action read. New tests: definedness_nested::an_action_sharing_a_chain_members_full_name_fails_closed, plus model-core unit tests for collisions and instance-like names. The corpus (6000 cases) generates collision actions at base and depth 1-3, exact or schema, with an independent oracle rule; the oracle orders action bases by shallowest member name; collision_decisive=65. The new hand and corpus tests fail on an export of 5aec4627. C018 regenerated. just check: governance stops only on GOV-4-06 security-review-present (lead-owned); all other recipes pass, with dossier/lean/test-policy run separately."}	blake3:4fq12vQaXe1FgAzm5pWGBRr-S5uSjO-yxgCZoIxHDJ8
1790288878277019	continuum-dev	itc:v3:AWKSTzM5JJnJPkQAAAAAQar23VW6voAAAAEythc		item.comment	bn-18w74	{"body":"cr-2qu5zr round 2 fixed at 4812c023. Every traversed symlink, on the walk and on every recheck: (1) its containing directory has no group/other write bits, sticky or not; (2) st_nlink == 1 (LinkedAncestor). Store files already required nlink 1 (HardLinked). The store dir must now be private (no group/other bits), so nobody else can name its files. Tests: sticky-dir symlink refused (earlier test converted into the guard), /tmp symlink refused, a hard-linked symlink refused and restored after unlink, private chains still work, a 0750 store refused. The hard-link acceptance residual is removed from docs and ADR; FUSE and an availability-only hard-link limit are stated. The adversarial pass found no blockers; its should-fixes and nits are done (private store dir, availability limit documented, UnsafeParent text). just check run recipe by recipe in the foreground: only the lead-owned security-review-present (T09 review gates) fails."}	blake3:ppiNGYvLD4JqCT1dO-B9uB0hvMHQozpbCh7STW9dG3U
1790290343036784	continuum-dev	itc:v3:AWKSTzM5JJnJPkQAAAAAQar23VW6voAAAAEytxc		item.comment	bn-34mw	{"body":"Committed f8a3e7f5 in ws bn-34mw. continuum-corpus gains src/differential (Engine adapter trait, normalized semantics, replay oracle, independent closure oracle, ddmin, defect_* report, LANES->docs/18 claims, quarantine ledger + gate); adapters for reference / kernel (wire-epoch-2 certs, claim bound to model+property) / semantic oracle in tests; register crates/continuum-corpus/differential/quarantine.txt (empty). Corpus 64 seeds + Die Hard: closure/kernel/semantic lanes 0 disagreements (pinned counts); explicit+DPOR lanes report absent. Planted mutants (lost transition, forged witness, laundered budget) detected, quarantine C006, gate fails vs baseline (C006 OBSERVED), 1-minimal fixtures re-verified. Test-only proved via cargo metadata kinds with injected-edge negatives. No new crates.io deps; C018 evidence regenerated. just check: all pass except lead-owned GOV-4-06 security-review-present (and T09 review-gates, which cites it; probe confirmed it is the only cause)."}	blake3:fR5IKAG80olt2ZBtIbVCNwGCsXpylPaDQlP0IvMlM94
