1790293979513214	continuum-dev	itc:v3:AWKSTzM5JJnJPkQAAAAAQar23VW6voAAAAEy0xc		item.comment	bn-34mw	{"body":"cr-2r0m24 round 2 committed: EngineError is a fault on either side or both (new EngineFaultBoth -> defect_*, ddmin, quarantine); typed inconclusives on both sides stay undecided; fault fields no longer counted undecided; panic attribution fixed; kernel Oversized -> Unsupported. Pinned corpus counts unchanged (0 faults before and after). Tests: the_same_engine_error_on_both_sides_is_a_defect (flipped), engine_faults_on_both_sides_are_reported_and_quarantined, a_typed_inconclusive_on_both_sides_is_undecided, panic_attribution_holds_with_a_faulty_or_panicking_other_side. Opus adversarial pass on delta: 5 findings, all fixed. just check: pass except lead-owned GOV-4-06 security-review-present (T09 review-gates cites it; probe confirmed)."}	blake3:oT3sKEKbWCTnpW6XRbZo6S8a7u-zwRm6BE98Z9Jf4UM
1790294036966669	continuum-dev	itc:v3:AWKSTzM5JJnJPkQAAAAAQar23VW6voAAAAEy1Bc		item.comment	bn-3snfi	{"body":"Delivered at 6e785051 (ws, not merged). Held bundles an import verified and the import records live in the keystore state file v2 (CTMSTA02; v1 read as no bundles); an import commits facts+bundle+records in one custody write (commit_import: NotRecorded rolls back all, Unconfirmed answers OutcomeUnknown + quarantine, nothing new writes nothing). Launch re-validates before sweep (restore_imports: bounds charged first, decode, identity recompute, self-signature, attested links, records resolve to canonical well-formed in_, every adopted link carried; refusals HeldBundle/ImportRecord/UncarriedLink) and re-enters records at proposed. No IDL/error-set change: export and reject write nothing (exported-only bundles stay memory-only; a rejected import re-enters after restart). Tests: bundle_custody.rs (9), signing_custody +1, keystore +4 and round trip extended. TEST-9-07 absence/evidence and ADR-0054 updated; GOV record tools/governance/reviews/bn-3snfi.toml without security table. Opus pass: no blockers; S1/S2 stated in ADR, N2 fixed, S3 (IDL rule prose) left to lead. just check recipe by recipe: all pass except lead-owned security-review-present (T09 review gates)."}	blake3:69-N9a99UG2-m60dqNniaSwkqepL3bgpiq7KhcIxggU
1790294076484782	continuum-dev	itc:v3:AWKSTzM5JJnJPkQAAAAAQar23VW6voAAAAEy1Rc		item.create	bn-2n6ol	{"description":"bn-3snfi persists held bundles in the keystore state file; bundles are never evicted, so the bounds hold across restarts and each custody write rewrites the whole state (up to 64 MiB). Design eviction (e.g. after acceptance or rejection, or by age) under the custody discipline, or split bundle storage from the key state.","kind":"task","labels":["phase-b","req:phase-b","security","risk:high"],"title":"Held intent bundles: eviction or garbage collection so the 1024-bundle / 64 MiB bound does not become permanent and every signing write stops rewriting up to 64 MiB (bn-3snfi follow-up)"}	blake3:XFnKxvvsahV-gqJNekWXdtqQG7c-sgjWyLPeZg--MdQ
1790294076684186	continuum-dev	itc:v3:AWKSTzM5JJnJPkQAAAAAQar23VW6voAAAAEy1hc		item.create	bn-33sey	{"description":"bn-3snfi: intent.reject does not persist and the intent registry is not persisted, so a rejected import returns at proposed after restart (still only acceptable through its bundle). Making reject durable adds a custody write, so intent.reject would need PublicationAborted/OutcomeUnknown in its error set: an IDL change, which in Phase B is a user decision.","kind":"task","labels":["phase-b","req:phase-b"],"title":"Decide whether intent.reject (and the intent registry) become durable across restart (bn-3snfi follow-up; IDL error-set change needs the user)"}	blake3:TLo4gvKrnuenvoJR1qTP6X-nitGlgeybZTwrIQUapeo
