1790296758317211	continuum-dev	itc:v3:AWKSTzM5JJnJPkQAAAAAQar23VW6voAAAAEy5hc		item.comment	bn-7xz8v	{"body":"cr-88az2y fixed at fbec8818. ServerReject::gated is the one constructor of RejectFrame, which has a private field and reads since::SERVER_REJECT. Server::open and Refusal.frame take only RejectFrame, so an ungated frame does not compile where a frame is sent. Both the negotiation and capability paths use gated, and the hard-coded 3.1 is gone. The guard now checks structure: the RejectFrame constructor, the emission signatures, and emitted_at on the private dispatch body and on refuse. Tests at 3.0/3.1 cover both reject paths. Correction 62 notes the gate. just check exit 0."}	blake3:FXcjSvMLeovQ_V9dKbI0HeFXgEubSEsbbhQpxlbq8_c
