1790299286815232	continuum-dev	itc:v3:AWKSTzM5JJnJPkQAAAAAQar23VW6voAAAAEy8Rc		item.comment	bn-34mw	{"body":"cr-2r0m24 round 5 committed: DefectReport encodes faults (fault.slot/fault.evidence, format /2), handle over them; ledger derived only from report content; HarnessError::DuplicateLane (engine-free). Tests: every_ledger_entry_names_a_report_encoding_its_evidence (property over trunk, tight budget, 7 mutants, contract fault, reference-slot evaluation faults; checks slot/side consistency of each fault line), two_transient_slots_each_rest_on_their_own_encoded_fault. Opus pass: 5 findings, all fixed. just check: pass except lead-owned GOV-4-06 (probe confirmed)."}	blake3:Zxm6hZL9SAgsi7prb0P0H72sWjLq6sd4F9a5lBARdZI
1790299378774536	continuum-dev	itc:v3:AWKSTzM5JJnJPkQAAAAAQar23VW6voAAAAEy8hc		item.comment	bn-1eoco	{"body":"95f2f6f7: continuum-incremental's engine.rs (check_invariant, domain_safety, Validated witness's engine-side scan) and audit.rs (verdict, undefined_action) call continuum_model_core::definedness::Definedness::of directly instead of a re-derived depth-1 X#defined scan. Both agree with engine-reference's checker by construction; audit's use of Definedness is model semantics, not engine decision logic, so tests/independence.rs's pin still holds unchanged. tests/differential.rs's Undefined comparison is real for whatever chain shape the oracle reports; depth-1 scope note removed from it and lib.rs; gains a two-actions case and an alpha-renaming metamorphic test. Nested chains, gaps and collisions (CML lowering never nests a #defined chain, so only a hand-built model carries them) are covered by new differential unit tests inside engine.rs's and audit.rs's own test modules, each checked against continuum-engine-reference's checking::check over a hand-built ModelBuilder model. Fresh opus adversarial pass: found and fixed one real defect (the definedness-classification charge undercounted building the action-name set once action_count exceeded ~8x predicate count); also fixed a misleading test comment/case (index-is-never-a-chain-member claim untested against the oracle's is_guard divergence) and a collision test checking only one of two relevant invariant names. GOV-4 review record tools/governance/reviews/bn-1eoco.toml added (security_review left out, lead-owned). Adds a direct continuum-model-core Cargo dependency (already transitive); dependency-rationale.toml used_by updated; C018 TCB evidence regenerated (Cargo.toml/Cargo.lock changed). just check: fmt/lint/test/boundaries/covenant pass; governance fails only on the expected GOV-4-06 security-review-present cascade (review gates control in check_t09_evidence.py); dossier, lean, test-policy pass when run separately. All prior goldens (reuse_spike, precision_baseline) unchanged."}	blake3:2N1QXg_GR_q_ChBIiWoK7T3mQkZmGt33Khxk39z97Iw
1790300712690673	continuum-dev	itc:v3:AWKSTzM5JJnJPkQAAAAAQar23VW6voAAAAEy8xc		item.comment	bn-2d70	{"body":"IMPL-01 committed f9f5ed9f in ws bn-2d70. Hypothesis follows schema+RFC 0032 corr.12: untrusted prose string, parsed by nothing. continuum-repair: handle/hypothesis/transaction modules; begin resolves base triple via FailureBinding seam (typed UnknownFailure/UnboundBaseSnapshot/BindingUnavailable); apply records hypothesis, refuses intent-kind change IntentMutationDenied; ID5 bytes, rt_ identity excl. repair_id, RepairTransaction<H>. Tests: pr20_impl01_hypothesis_evidence.rs (10) + fixtures pr20-impl01-ack-after-sync-{draft,applied} registered in validate_dossier. inv001 pin converted to regression guard. just check: only failure is lead-owned GOV-4-06 security-review-present (surfaces via check_t09 review gates); dossier/lean/test-policy pass when run after it. Open: two begins on one crashpack mint one rt_ (schema has no discriminator); status in preimage vs later superseded."}	blake3:9nUFEORKQcp36YiSBZ6FKOGHsHZWjAHhtJS7zr2y1-o
1790301310779816	continuum-dev	itc:v3:AWKSTzM5JJnJPkQAAAAAQar23VW6voAAAAEy9Bc		item.comment	bn-voq4	{"body":"Definedness (RFC 0003) in continuum-engine-dpor at 500e5017: undefined reads typed via model-core Definedness in the reference precedence; consulted definedness predicates' reads visible (soundness argued in lib.rs, hidden-undefined adversarial model + hide-definedness-reads mutant); checker scans definedness the same way; C005 differential compares undefined reads against oracle-marked states, exact vs checker, 652 comparisons; ledger/docs updated; C018 evidence regenerated (sync had left a conflict in c018.json). just check: only lead-owned traceability staleness."}	blake3:YRJbhHcptQxmdd3Ru8QmXI4l_XGlRIVMaAP-TVFWFsE
1790302313551749	continuum-dev	itc:v3:AWKSTzM5JJnJPkQAAAAAQar23VW6voAAAAEy9Rc		item.comment	bn-3km4z	{"body":"PR 18 deletion + causal closure landed in ws bn-3km4z (commits efe36125, 914de4ea, plus rationale). Generic passes: crates/continuum-debugger/src/reduce.rs (closure of witnesses; ddmin over configurations or atoms; oracle replay of every kept set; budget charged first; typed ResourceExhausted/EngineError inconclusive; CausallyMinimal/OneMinimal/AtomMinimal only when all final removals decided). PR-14 journal instantiation: crates/continuum-asupersync/src/causal.rs (footprint dependence, operation atoms, first-appearance permute/restrict). Evidence pr18-impl01-01..05 in crates/continuum-asupersync/tests/golden/pr18_impl01_reduction.evidence.txt: M01 Agreement 137->89, AckedNotDurable 97->40, mechanism kept, causally closed and causally minimal; 400-run corpus closure checked pairwise, median core 54%; adjacent independent swaps lift; atoms-mode ddmin reaches 7.7% but loses the mechanism under a substrate replay (pinned). Tests: 12 in continuum-debugger/tests/pr18_reduce.rs, 13 in pr18_impl01_reduction.rs. GOV record tools/governance/reviews/bn-3km4z.toml without security_review. just check: all gates pass except governance security-review-present (lead-owned; also surfaces as t09 review gates); dossier, lean, test-policy run by hand after it, pass."}	blake3:t1GtfZbpHMcXFA-D8G15b0Z3U87bk9h0F3JJab8E1RM
1790302460219517	continuum-dev	itc:v3:AWKSTzM5JJnJPkQAAAAAQar23VW6voAAAAEy9hc		item.create	bn-13zbn	{"description":"bn-2d70: RFC 0032 says repair_id is the content identity and that two distinct begins are two transactions; repair-transaction.schema.json (additionalProperties false) has no field to tell them apart, so two begins on one crashpack mint the same rt_. Decide the RFC/schema fix (e.g. a begin nonce/ordinal in the preimage, or begin is idempotent by design and the RFC sentence is corrected). A schema epoch change may need the user.","kind":"task","labels":["phase-b","req:phase-b","req:pr-20"],"title":"Repair transaction identity: two begins on one crashpack mint the same rt_ (RFC 0032 contradiction; schema has no distinguishing field) (bn-2d70 finding)"}	blake3:mZqtlUd52hY3rTIfg3NCREvy6YdkRPgaje32MMu3R7I
1790302460430665	continuum-dev	itc:v3:AWKSTzM5JJnJPkQAAAAAQar23VW6voAAAAEy9xc		item.create	bn-85li6	{"description":"bn-2d70: status participates in the rt_ preimage. ADR-0018: a published artifact never mutates. IMPL-06 (policy verdict) must decide whether superseded is kept outside the published artifact or status leaves the preimage (RFC 0032/schema).","kind":"task","labels":["phase-b","req:phase-b","req:pr-20"],"title":"Repair transaction: status is inside the identity preimage, so a later superseded status would change a published version's bytes (bn-2d70 finding, PR-20 IMPL-06 seam)"}	blake3:tGGOjj72E1xE7TTgQ0n3LGOAt6kUzo29o3RuWeLrks0
1790302460628912	continuum-dev	itc:v3:AWKSTzM5JJnJPkQAAAAAQar23VW6voAAAAEy-Bc		item.create	bn-23pwm	{"description":"bn-2d70 delivered the library (continuum-repair RepairTransaction::begin/apply with UnknownFailure, UnboundBaseSnapshot, BindingUnavailable, IntentMutationDenied). repair.begin/apply are not served; library-only is partial. Wire them, with BindingUnavailable distinct from UnknownFailure on the wire (INV-008), compare-and-set on the lineage head, and a daemon-set hypothesis size bound. If the IDL error sets need a new code, that is a protocol minor for the user.","kind":"task","labels":["phase-b","req:phase-b","req:pr-20","security","risk:high"],"title":"Wire repair.begin and repair.apply into continuumd, mapping RepairTransaction's typed refusals onto the IDL error sets (bn-2d70 follow-up)"}	blake3:xJHh_-NWd2MmsCF2sJtc6tN9GJj_-WS1Nibw_UQSi60
1790302460832085	continuum-dev	itc:v3:AWKSTzM5JJnJPkQAAAAAQar23VW6voAAAAEy-Rc		item.create	bn-2z08o	{"description":"bn-3km4z: the replay oracle (lift + A7 model + projection) checks substrate semantics, not the program's, so ddmin over atoms reaches 7.7% but loses the mechanism (no Submit kept in 400/400). The M01 core is 65%/41% of the trace via configuration deletion, not compact. Add a program-level replay oracle (the register's own protocol/property checks) so atom deletion is faithful, and record RFC 0028's per-removal transcript. PR-18 exit (bn-2nh6) stays partial until then.","kind":"task","labels":["phase-b","req:phase-b","req:pr-18"],"title":"PR 18: program-level replay oracle so atom-level deletion keeps the causal mechanism, and per-removal minimizer transcripts (RFC 0028) (bn-3km4z follow-up)"}	blake3:e2aS1znxJ-UgS1MOZhSDlA3K5TCBR4fmXC9ObLLqOZ0
1790302461025802	continuum-dev	itc:v3:AWKSTzM5JJnJPkQAAAAAQar23VW6voAAAAEy-hc		item.create	bn-3ncgl	{"description":"bn-3km4z's closure/deletion passes are library-only (continuum-debugger reduce.rs). failure.minimize is unserved; wire it in continuumd over a crashpack's journal, typed Inconclusive on budget, with the core as a retained artifact. IDL: check the operation's declared shape; no protocol change without the user.","kind":"task","labels":["phase-b","req:phase-b","req:pr-18"],"title":"Serve failure.minimize: a production caller for the PR 18 reduction passes (bn-3km4z follow-up)"}	blake3:jzXqmc8mNObCB25RVH0k8doPKoS6AYnTkTnSTvcSO3I
