1790306426947083	continuum-dev	itc:v3:AWKSTzM5JJnJPkQAAAAAQar23VW6voAAAAEypBg		item.comment	bn-4ykgg	{"body":"PR 21 neighbor generation landed in ws bn-4ykgg (commits 10c41699, ccaaa452, 8cc21fa6, plus C018 regen). crates/continuum-repair/src/neighborhood.rs: RFC 0032's 8 strategies. Generic generators over a CausalCore trait: schedule-perturbation, alternate-enabled-events, message delay/dup/loss. Substrate hooks for fault-window, cancellation-checkpoints and value-name-permutation. Each candidate is typed against the Intent Contract FaultModel/Bounds plus scenario caps and against the causal order before it runs. Rejections are typed and counted, never realized. Budget is charged before work (ResourceExhausted with frontier). Record is canonical JSON (crate-local continuum.repair.neighborhood/v0). Receipt projection conforms to promotion-receipt coverage.neighborhood and is refused on undecided or unnamed runs. Register instantiation on M01's scenario core (op-grain causal closure): 99 candidates, 80 valid, 72 executed per program. Correct passes all 72 (46 distinct runs). M01 fails 66 (62 distinct). Evidence pr21-impl01-01..05. Adversarial opus pass done; findings fixed. just check: all green except the lead-owned GOV-4-06 security-review-present (via check_obligations and t09 review gates). Follow-ups: CIR core, PR18 deletion core feed-in, network dup/loss on the register, and wiring into the PR20 gate 5."}	blake3:OfwZ5GQCzabnVRcp4jMGgueZc5evqqWyrP8BSbVeu2Y
