1790307422875684	continuum-dev	itc:v3:AWKSTzM5JJnJPkQAAAAAQar23VW6voAAAAEyqxg		item.comment	bn-195b	{"body":"IMPL-02 committed 2308e4f2 in ws bn-195b. New crates/continuum-repair/src/patch.rs: SealedCandidate::seal derives the candidate from base content + DeclaredChange edits (Create / Replace{before} / Delete{before}) via continuum-workspace Snapshot; unchecked_from removed; apply(proposal, base) records derived candidate_snapshot and changes[].digest (<alg>:<hex> of canonical change record), least-path canonical order, path-disjoint changes. Typed refusals BaseMismatch, StaleBefore, MissingFile, NotAFile, CreateOverExisting, OverlappingChanges, Tree; SealedCandidate::check -> UndeclaredEdits. Tests: tests/pr20_impl02_patch_identity.rs (9), IMPL-01 suite re-blessed with derived handles. TCB c018 evidence regenerated. just check: all recipes pass except governance security-review-present (lead-owned). Open: RFC 0032 names no wire code for apply-time patch refusals; bn-23pwm maps them."}	blake3:wJfGIZkeF-M3eQPKTIIlhqa5OrclOWcfRY7t4GqC4oc
1790307454973184	continuum-dev	itc:v3:AWKSTzM5JJnJPkQAAAAAQar23VW6voAAAAEyrBg		item.comment	bn-23pwm	{"body":"From bn-195b: RFC 0032/IDL name no wire code for apply-time PatchRefusal (BaseMismatch, StaleBefore, MissingFile, NotAFile, CreateOverExisting, OverlappingChanges, Tree, UndeclaredEdits); repair.apply's union is IntentMutationDenied + UnsupportedSemanticFeature + common codes, and the RFC does not state the path-disjointness rule. Needs an RFC 0032 correction (and, if a new code is needed, a protocol minor = user decision). Also: carry DeclaredChange over the IDL Opaque changes, resolve base content from the store, publish candidate records, and a durable store of declared change payloads so gate 2 can re-seal a published version."}	blake3:Qcc24lkeIOPJWALEQgsU9wLChE87em8iMShUEsFT8pE
