1790310792719643	continuum-dev	itc:v3:AWKSTzM5JJnJPkQAAAAAQar23VW6voAAAAEytBg		item.comment	bn-jw7q	{"body":"PR-15-EXIT evidence in ws bn-jw7q, commit c3299269. New crates/continuum-asupersync/tests/pr15_exit_evidence.rs (16 tests), golden tests/golden/pr15_exit_evidence.txt, and summary tests/evidence/pr15-exit.json. Artifact ids are pr15-exit-{hon,pos,neg,bnd}-NN. Window classes come from each pack's CANCELLATION_CONTRACT. The process pack routes cancellation to the runtime. The time pack has no operation. Crash outcomes come from enabled_choices at every boundary: 7 seeds, 2 configs per pack. Each window is replayed from its bytes by an independent decoder, from its plan, and by Journal::replay. Counts: network 798 cancel points; process 2,400 crash windows; storage 5,382 crash windows and 798 cancel points; composed 2,386; register 72 graceful and 72 fail-stop over 7 lab seeds. All 8 retained PR-16 correct-baseline campaigns reproduce their golden identities and counts. Every moved or dropped crash or cancellation is a typed divergence. Unsupported cases are typed refusals. The verdict fails closed. Dev edges to the 4 packs have GOV-1-07 rationale entries, and c018 TCB evidence is regenerated. No src change. START_HERE annotated and traceability regenerated. The opus review found 0 blockers, 6 should-fix and 7 nits; all are fixed or stated as narrowing. just check exit 0."}	blake3:JUxgWe3Ew1eNwrh3Vk7i_TeuwBaWbyGC0pe99FYaIf4
