1790313881845107	continuum-dev	itc:v3:AWKSTzM5JJnJPkQAAAAAQar23VW6voAAAAEyzBg		item.comment	bn-3vhzw	{"body":"Committed bb3fe801 in ws bn-3vhzw. Added DporEngine (fills the DPOR-vs-tiny-oracle lane, absent since bn-34mw) in crates/continuum-corpus/tests/support/engines.rs: maps dpor::check onto Normalized; Projection::Exact only when Complete and the reduction's visible mask covers every variable (else Unsupported, never laundered); an EngineError the deadlock question itself carries is checked ahead of completeness/mask so it always enters the defect lifecycle (fixed after opus review found the original order masked it). Corpus run (81 fixtures): agreed=53, disagreements=0, pinned; a direct Stats check proves the lane's exact-set fixtures are provably unreduced (declined_persistent=declined_sleep=0 whenever the mask is full), documented as evidence about DPOR's search machinery, not its reduction (continuum-engine-dpor's own bn-voq4 differential already tests the reduction exhaustively). DporLostState (wrapper mutant; the crate's own mutants are #[cfg(test)]-private, confirmed unreachable) drops one discovered state: detected on 31/81 fixtures, minimized, quarantines C005 (OBSERVED, unregistered) -- pinned. continuum-engine-dpor added as continuum-corpus dev-dependency only; dependency-rationale.toml entry added; tools/check_tcb_audit.py --evidence rerun (Cargo.lock changed). Opus adversarial review: 6 findings, 3 fixed (fault-masking bug, pinned mutant disagreeing-fixtures=31, added the Stats regression test replacing an assertion that was structurally impossible to satisfy), 1 documented in code (masking argument correct but full-mask fixtures exercise no actual reduction), 2 deferred to the lead (adding a second DPOR-vs-REFERENCE lane with Fields::ALL both sides so the 30 masked fixtures' verdicts are cross-checked too -- out of scope for an adapter-only bone since it changes the LANES table; the .expect() in dpor_trace is defensible, panics are caught and typed by the harness). just check: PASS (fmt, lint, test, boundaries, covenant, governance, dossier, lean, test-policy)."}	blake3:6lmjp-nt6ufv1SzlP6fuRY2BPDLn0rgicYQtnbDC5Io
1790313927144246	continuum-dev	itc:v3:AWKSTzM5JJnJPkQAAAAAQar23VW6voAAAAEyzRg		item.create	bn-2vuya	{"description":"bn-3vhzw: (a) the DPOR vs tiny-oracle lane compares exact projections only on full-mask fixtures, where DPOR's reduction is provably inactive; add a DPOR vs REFERENCE lane (Fields::ALL both sides) so masked fixtures' verdicts get a cross-engine check; (b) the harness lets an engine that answers Inconclusive everywhere pass a lane vacuously; add a LaneCounts/gate rule that a lane with zero decided comparisons is Vacuous, never green. Touches the governed LANES table.","kind":"task","labels":["phase-b","req:phase-b","req:c005"],"title":"Cross-engine harness: a DPOR-vs-reference lane with full fields, and a harness-level guard against lanes that pass vacuously on Inconclusive-everywhere engines (bn-3vhzw follow-ups)"}	blake3:IkTkBx57QkLVDbcQnKB2Bze2VVtAuhoUoR0rxhq2kog
