1790316183954270	continuum-dev	itc:v3:AWKSTzM5JJnJPkQAAAAAQar23VW6voAAAAEy2xg		item.comment	bn-4ykgg	{"body":"cr-3hfw5b fixes: c179f758 plus the adversarial follow-up 5f5e28a9. (1) Records have private fields and no constructor. Each is bound to Inputs: generator, rt_ transaction, candidate subject, engine identity, core commitment over the whole relation, core profile, envelope, config, plus a per-neighbor content commitment. receipt_coverage(substrate, envelope, config) derives the current Inputs itself and refuses Stale/Inconsistent/Pending, then any terminal state other than Complete. reconcile() ties every count, the run and candidate spend, the not_realizable reasons, and descriptive fields vs binding. (2) Continuation bytes are never trusted: resume_bytes and the public decode are removed. resume_untrusted runs a fresh derivation and returns Forged on any differing committed neighbor, including a coherent fail-to-pass rewrite. (3) In-memory resume regenerates every committed candidate and compares id, commitment and rejection (Diverged/Mismatch on engine, core or scenario-content change). (4) The register executes a neighbor only when its realization passes same_interleaving: exact for M01, unaffected cross-actor pairs for the correct program, and truncated runs refused. The correct program's constraint is disclosed (12 of 283 pairs, 0 dependent). Explored is projected as distinct runs. (5) MEDIUMs: Pending checked first; the scenario id charge is taken back; checked sums; a selected strategy with 0 candidates is a gap. just check: green except the lead-owned GOV-4-06 security-review-present."}	blake3:GvG3Hk5fepJKJfz6InxA8BCEqpCTOhBDXQ4QJob2quo
1790316224674065	continuum-dev	itc:v3:AWKSTzM5JJnJPkQAAAAAQar23VW6voAAAAEy3Bg		item.create	bn-xa8c2	{"description":"bn-4ykgg cr-3hfw5b: (1) for the correct program, same_interleaving constrains only 12 of 283 cross-actor core pairs (disclosed); a Mazurkiewicz-trace equivalence over a relation shared across program versions would make the check library-side; (2) resuming a neighborhood campaign across a restart without re-running needs the daemon's authenticated cont_ store (resume_untrusted re-derives everything today).","kind":"task","labels":["phase-b","req:phase-b","req:pr-21"],"title":"PR 21: library-level trace-equivalence check for neighbors across program versions, and a daemon-authenticated cont_ store for neighborhood continuations (bn-4ykgg follow-ups)"}	blake3:RvQnzp9SQ0MTMtjUv7ap8_y4X8lV8TgJ9p4NvKtygvk
1790316224716687	continuum-dev	itc:v3:AWKSTzM5JJnJPkQAAAAAQar23VW6voAAAAEy3Rg		item.link	bn-xa8c2	{"link_type":"blocks","target":"bn-19p"}	blake3:00nDpAfY1N26OSnkGYfI7vF6P8du5ym5ot6Z9DxwjYw
