1790316271302957	continuum-dev	itc:v3:AWKSTzM5JJnJPkQAAAAAQar23VW6voAAAAEy3xg		item.comment	bn-2pla	{"body":"IMPL-03 committed 453b3f9e in ws bn-2pla. New crates/continuum-repair/src/replay.rs: replay::evaluate checks crash_ identity of the crashpack bytes (CrashpackTampered), strict RecordedRun decode, base/candidate content ids, then records gates 1 and 4 as the next version with crash_/ev_/defect_ evidence naming the Replayer. Gate 1: exact run passes; failure absent or different fails; divergence or failure-without-the-run is inconclusive EngineError with defect_. Gate 4: no failure passes, a failure fails, divergence inconclusive; not run (stays pending) when gate 1 does not pass. Eliminated positions and reordered count are disclosed. Status derives evaluating. Tests: continuum-repair tests/pr20_impl03_exact_replay.rs (15); continuum-asupersync tests/pr20_impl03_exact_replay.rs (10) on M01: 400/400 base exact and ack-after-sync passes, no-fix recurs 400/400, double-ack diverges 400/400, tampered refused; 3 evaluated versions checked by validate_dossier. Adversarial opus pass: 3 blockers, 7 should-fix, 6 nits; fixed B3,S1,S2,S3,S6,S7,N4, disclosed S4 (reordered count), softened S5, raised B1/B2 as RFC open questions. just check: all recipes pass except governance review gates (security-review-present, lead-owned). C018 evidence regenerated."}	blake3:hS05qauhAH6FgJaiZqS1XFgjreSHe8vbddH_Lp9petA
1790316308498395	continuum-dev	itc:v3:AWKSTzM5JJnJPkQAAAAAQar23VW6voAAAAEy4Bg		item.create	bn-2vanm	{"description":"bn-2pla: (B1) gate 4 (exact_regression) passes with eliminated recorded steps; no evaluation_policy is declared anywhere; the ack-after-sync repair removes exactly the early ack the failure needed, so treating elimination as inconclusive would block the fix. Decide the policy in an RFC 0032 correction. (B2) RFC 0032 makes semantic_diff non-null from evaluating onward, but a persisted partial campaign (gates 1 and 4 recorded, IMPL-04 diff not yet) is evaluating with semantic_diff null; the schema accepts it, the RFC table does not. (3) How a crashpack manifest id binds the RecordedRun identity (no crashpack producer yet). If a correction changes a ratified gate, it goes to the user.","kind":"task","labels":["phase-b","req:phase-b","req:pr-20"],"title":"RFC 0032 gaps from exact replay: gate-4 evaluation_policy for eliminated steps (flag F3), and semantic_diff non-null from evaluating vs a partial campaign (bn-2pla findings)"}	blake3:mCSKS0ZPSatyx7O9CfR7J32xwRaCmU2RSZXermf_G8A
