1790316753672765	continuum-dev	itc:v3:AWKSTzM5JJnJPkQAAAAAQar23VW6voAAAAEy4xg		item.comment	bn-25z9o	{"body":"Owner/fault/value reduction in ws bn-25z9o (commit 733c3894). New continuum-debugger/src/scenario.rs: reduces a run's configuration, not its events. Rounds of owner, fault and value passes, greedy to a fixpoint. Each pass declares Property/Defect/Semantics/Bounds (INV-013) or is refused; out-of-scope candidates are recorded, never run. The engine keeps its own observed measures (contract breach on a non-decrease), charges before work, and returns typed inconclusives and an RFC 0028 transcript. Minimality classes need a complete transcript and a fully decided last round. Register instantiation: tests/pr18_impl02_scenario_reduction.rs. Each candidate is built as M01's plan (build_pruned for owners) and run through the binding, using the original order carried over (guided_log), then a seeded search; a sampled miss is Inconclusive. Schedule-free Holds need fewer than two acking coordinators; 11 such configs were checked on schedules. The composed core then gets bn-2z08o closure+deletion. Agreement witness: already Owner/Fault/Value-minimal, 93/137. AND witness: replica c dropped, core 42 (43.3% of 97). Corpus of 400: 358 AND runs lose c and a's crash; all keep the mechanism. Median core is 31.5% of the original run and 59.2% of the reduced run: PR-18 exit NOT MET, bn-2nh6 not marked. Minimization cost: median 151 binding executions per failure against the campaign's 2925. Evidence: pr18-impl02-01..08. Shared register instantiation moved to tests/support/pr18_program.rs; impl01 goldens are unchanged. GOV record tools/governance/reviews/bn-25z9o.toml, without security_review. just check: fmt, lint, test, boundaries, covenant, lean and test-policy pass. governance fails only on security-review-present and t09 review gates (lead-owned). dossier fails only on PLAN_BONE_TRACEABILITY staleness (lead-owned)."}	blake3:hhlAF6QqEF_Aywqo1pPMeYZLH0aDgEaqmmATwT1VSzg
1790316805806819	continuum-dev	itc:v3:AWKSTzM5JJnJPkQAAAAAQar23VW6voAAAAEy5Bg		item.comment	bn-25z9o	{"body":"Review anchor: 01M3BK4ZJHYZCC1J4HPPJDZ4KS for cr-3k3658 (security review, head d986a48e6ee0)"}	blake3:l_E7wtDw6vnvbqO2J7XOafXlOfg1VUpyv149KvTWL7k
1790317781177499	continuum-dev	itc:v3:AWKSTzM5JJnJPkQAAAAAQar23VW6voAAAAEy5Rg		item.comment	bn-9r5e	{"body":"IMPL-05 in ws bn-9r5e, head 8f98f81b. New crates/continuum-repair/src/receipt/status.rs. RefinementCertificateStatus is derived from a new CandidateEvidence daemon seam at compose and at verify. A certificate counts only when its ModelBound verdict names the candidate itself (the bn-3hk4v path). 13 typed Unverified reasons cover the rest. Refinement and rebuild coverage are typed Absent. A claimed coverage.refinement_coverage or certificate_rebuild group is CoverageNotDerived. Gate 8 or 9 listed passed is GateWithoutEvidence. Every profile enforces gate 8, so no receipt verifies until PR 17 ships a checker. Tests: tests/pr22_impl05_impl06_evidence.rs plus the receipt::tests::pr22_impl05_* unit tests. Fixture pr22-impl05-ack-after-sync-certificate-status. GOV record tools/governance/reviews/bn-9r5e.toml. just check: all recipes pass except two lead-owned items: governance security-review-present / T09 review gates, and dossier PLAN_BONE_TRACEABILITY staleness from bone state."}	blake3:BPpo2HElPl-3nlxUF7AhX0ePbQjhX_EmbQLvH35K87s
1790317781213932	continuum-dev	itc:v3:AWKSTzM5JJnJPkQAAAAAQar23VW6voAAAAEy5hg		item.comment	bn-yzu1	{"body":"IMPL-06 in ws bn-9r5e, head 8f98f81b, together with bn-9r5e. New crates/continuum-repair/src/receipt/unknowns.rs. Unknowns is derived from the gate record, the IMPL-05 status and the declared pack cases, one entry per input. The token grammar is injective, and from_token inverts it. Canonical order is byte order. Verify refuses an omitted, invented, duplicated or reordered entry, and an absent unknowns. A completeness test checks every profile, gate status, verdict and pack set. A differential test runs against the continuum-effects-storage UNSUPPORTED table. Fixture pr22-impl06-ack-after-sync-unknowns. just check: same result as bn-9r5e."}	blake3:_R_nYUaVc0zYuxrNS1Jcw3VL76Ia6R5hbtkR3UpGnRY
1790321613577029	continuum-dev	itc:v3:AWKSTzM5JJnJPkQAAAAAQar23VW6voAAAAEy5xg		item.comment	bn-1ss	{"body":"CIR landed (85bee816 in ws bn-1ss). continuum-cir: cir-0.1 event identity, builder (causes = immediate predecessors under footprint+owner dependence; runs merged into a prime event structure with immediate conflicts), validator re-deriving every edge, strict budgeted cir.schema.json reader/writer. continuum-asupersync src/cir.rs lowers lift-admitted journals; adds alloc/<kind> writes (dense ordinals). Tests: crates/continuum-cir/tests/pr17_cir_semantics.rs (8), crates/continuum-asupersync/tests/pr17_impl01_cir.rs (7) + golden pr17-impl01-01..04, pr17-impl02-01..04; 29 merged docs pass jsonschema. GOV record tools/governance/reviews/bn-1ss.toml without security_review. just check: all green except lead-owned security-review-present (obligations and T09 review gates). Opus adversarial pass done, 7 of 10 findings fixed."}	blake3:FTFAhV5NYFH9NtS3cFzlV8E--ZOpwLqaccIcvn18vN0
1790350144429640	continuum-dev	itc:v3:AWKSTzM5JJnJPkQAAAAAQar23VW6voAAAAEy6Bg		item.comment	bn-2nh6	{"body":"User decision 2026-09-25 (research/26 kill check): the 31.5% corpus-median core (bn-25z9o; one experiment class, durability/ack-before-sync, 400 M01 runs, measured on raw PR-14 journal events) is recorded as a PROVISIONAL single-class measurement; the registered kill is NOT triggered. Remeasure when PR 17 CIR events exist and at least a second experiment class is in the corpus. PR-18 exit stays open."}	blake3:95WzjycCx7nnD46ZNmASKGdu0QqyHanoPw2nMenEojU
